  b:["PulseSpace is a wellness tool. Share any concerns with your doctor or midwife."],rel:['rhr']},
 {id:'kids',q:"Are the ranges the same for children or older adults?",kw:['child','children','kid','kids','baby','infant','elderly','senior','older adult','old age','teenager'],
  p:["No. PulseSpace uses adult ranges. Children have faster heart rates, and older adults often have lower HRV."],
  b:["For a child, use a pediatrician's guidance and a device made for children.","For older adults, compare against their own usual numbers."],rel:['rhr','hrvgood']},
 {id:'meds',q:"Do medicines change my heart rate?",kw:['medication','medicine','medicines','beta blocker','tablet','pill','prescription','steroid'],
  p:["Yes. Beta blockers and some heart medicines slow the pulse. Decongestants, asthma inhalers, thyroid tablets and caffeine-containing medicines can raise it."],
  b:["Do not change or stop any medicine because of a reading. Ask your doctor or pharmacist."],rel:['tachy','brady']},
 {id:'illness',q:"Can being sick affect my SpO2 and pulse?",kw:['flu','infection','pneumonia','sick','illness','viral'],
  p:["Yes. When you are ill, resting heart rate usually rises and HRV drops, sometimes a day or two before symptoms."],
  b:["With a chest or breathing illness, contact a doctor if SpO₂ stays below about 94% or you feel breathless.","Get urgent help for breathing difficulty at rest, a bluish tint or confusion."],rel:['lowspo2','bodytemp']},
 {id:'whenmeasure',q:"When is the best time to measure?",kw:['best time','when to measure','how often','how long should i measure','every day','daily','morning','before bed','after waking','same time'],
  p:["Measure at the same time each day, ideally in the morning after waking, before coffee, seated and rested for five minutes."],
  b:["Avoid measuring right after exercise, a meal or caffeine.","Trends over several days are more meaningful than any single reading."],rel:['variation','fingerpos']},
 {id:'variation',q:"Why do my readings change every time?",kw:['different readings','readings vary','readings change','reading change','fluctuate','fluctuating','inconsistent','not consistent','varies','vary'],
