E('dengue',"What are the symptoms of dengue?",['dengue','dengue fever','mosquito fever symptoms','mosquito fever','platelet count','platelets','breakbone fever'],
 ["Dengue is spread by mosquitoes. It causes sudden high fever, severe headache, pain behind the eyes, muscle and joint pain, nausea and sometimes a rash."],
 ["Get tested if you have these symptoms, especially during or after the rainy season.","Rest, drink plenty of fluids and use paracetamol for fever. Avoid aspirin and ibuprofen because they can raise the risk of bleeding.","Warning signs usually appear around day 3 to 7, as the fever falls: severe stomach pain, repeated vomiting, bleeding from the nose or gums, black stools, drowsiness or fast breathing. Go to a hospital immediately."],['monsoon','fevercare','malaria']);
E('malaria',"What are the symptoms of malaria?",['malaria','shivering fever','fever with chills','chills and shivering'],
 ["Malaria causes fever with chills and heavy sweating, headache and body aches, often in cycles. It is spread by mosquitoes and needs a blood test."],
 ["In areas where malaria occurs, get tested for any fever.","It is treatable with prescribed medicines. Delay can make it serious.","Prevent it with nets, repellents, long sleeves and getting rid of standing water."],['monsoon','dengue','fevercare']);
E('typhoid',"What are the symptoms of typhoid?",['typhoid','enteric fever','widal test','typhoid fever'],
 ["Typhoid is spread by contaminated food and water. It causes a fever that rises over several days, weakness, stomach pain, headache and either constipation or diarrhea."],
 ["A blood culture confirms it. Antibiotics from a doctor are needed.","Drink boiled or filtered water, eat freshly cooked food and wash hands often. A typhoid vaccine is available."],['diarrhea','fevercare']);
E('chikungunya',"What is chikungunya?",['chikungunya','chikungunya fever'],
 ["Chikungunya is spread by mosquitoes. It causes sudden fever and severe joint pain, often in the wrists, ankles and fingers, which can last for weeks."],
 ["Rest, drink fluids and use paracetamol. Avoid ibuprofen and aspirin until a doctor has ruled out dengue.","See a doctor if pain is severe, or if you are elderly, pregnant or have other conditions."],['dengue','monsoon']);
E('monsoon',"How do I stay healthy in the monsoon?",['monsoon','rainy season','mosquito bite','mosquito repellent','prevent mosquitoes','stagnant water','waterlogging'],
 ["Rain brings mosquito-borne and water-borne illnesses. A few habits cut the risk."],
 ["Remove standing water from pots, coolers and tyres every week.","Use nets, repellents and long sleeves, especially at dawn and dusk.","Drink boiled or filtered water and eat freshly cooked food. Wash fruit and vegetables well.","Dry your feet and shoes to prevent fungal infection, and change out of wet clothes quickly.","See a doctor for fever that lasts more than two days."],['dengue','malaria','typhoid']);
E('covid',"What are the symptoms of COVID-19?",['covid','coronavirus','covid 19','covid symptoms','corona'],
 ["COVID-19 can cause fever, cough, sore throat, tiredness, body aches and loss of smell or taste. Many cases are mild."],
 ["Rest, drink fluids and follow your local testing and isolation advice.","Your finger SpO₂ is a useful check. Get medical help if it stays below about 94%, or if you have trouble breathing, chest pain, confusion or bluish lips.","Older adults and people with long-term conditions should speak to a doctor early."],['illness','lowspo2','vaccines']);
E('jaundice',"What causes jaundice and liver problems?",['jaundice','yellow eyes','yellow skin','hepatitis','fatty liver','liver health','liver','liver damage'],
 ["Jaundice turns the skin and eyes yellow. It can come from hepatitis, gallstones, alcohol or some medicines, and it needs a doctor's check."],
 ["Dark urine, pale stools, itching, tiredness and stomach pain often come with it.","To protect your liver: limit alcohol, keep a healthy weight, get hepatitis vaccines and avoid unprescribed herbal or painkiller mixes.","Fatty liver is common and often improves with weight loss, exercise and cutting sugar."],['alcohol','weightloss']);
E('sinus',"How do I relieve a blocked nose and sinus pressure?",['sinus','sinusitis','blocked nose','nasal congestion','sinus pressure','stuffed nose','nose blocked'],
 ["Steam, warm fluids and a saline spray or rinse usually ease it. If you rinse your nose, use boiled and cooled or distilled water."],
 ["See a doctor if it lasts more than 10 days, with severe facial pain, high fever, or swelling around the eyes."],['coldflu','allergy']);
E('arthritis',"What helps joint stiffness and arthritis?",['arthritis','knee pain','joint pain','pain in knees','knee hurts','joint stiffness','swollen joints','rheumatoid','gout','uric acid','knee arthritis','joint swelling'],
 ["Osteoarthritis comes from wear on the joints. Rheumatoid arthritis is an immune condition, with morning stiffness lasting more than 30 minutes and swollen joints. Gout causes sudden, red, very painful swelling, often at the big toe."],
 ["Gentle exercise, a healthy weight, heat or cold packs and strengthening the muscles around the joint help.","For gout, limit alcohol (especially beer), red meat, organ meat and sugary drinks, and drink plenty of water.","See a doctor for hot, swollen joints, joint pain with fever, or stiffness that lasts weeks."],['backpain','exercise']);
E('osteo',"How can I keep my bones strong?",['osteoporosis','calcium','strong bones','bone health','bone density','weak bones','bone strength','brittle bones'],
 ["Bones stay strong with calcium, vitamin D, weight-bearing exercise and not smoking."],
 ["Adults need about 1,000 mg of calcium a day (more for women over 50 and men over 70).","Good sources are milk, curd, paneer, ragi, sesame, leafy greens and tofu.","Walk, climb stairs and do strength training. Get some sunlight.","Ask a doctor about a bone density scan if you are over 50, post-menopausal or have risk factors."],['vitamins','strength']);
E('piles',"What can I do about piles?",['piles','hemorrhoids','haemorrhoids','anal fissure','blood in stool','rectal bleeding'],
 ["Piles are swollen veins near the anus, usually from straining or low fibre."],
 ["Eat more fibre, drink water, avoid long sitting on the toilet and try a warm sitz bath.","Any rectal bleeding should be checked by a doctor. See one sooner for severe pain, or symptoms lasting more than a week."],['constipation','water']);
E('heel',"Why does my heel hurt?",['heel pain','plantar fasciitis','foot pain','flat feet','footwear','sore feet','pain in heel'],
 ["Heel pain that is worst with the first steps in the morning is often plantar fasciitis."],
 ["Stretch your calves and the sole of the foot, wear supportive shoes and avoid walking barefoot on hard floors.","See a doctor if it lasts more than a few weeks or you cannot put weight on the foot."],['running','backpain']);
E('numbness',"Why do I get tingling or numbness in my hands?",['numbness','tingling','pins and needles','numb hands','numb fingers','carpal tunnel','hand tingling','wrist pain'],
 ["Pins and needles often come from pressure on a nerve, such as sleeping on your arm. Carpal tunnel, low B12, diabetes and neck problems can also cause it."],
 ["Change position, shake out the hand and avoid resting on the wrist for long.","See a doctor if it keeps happening or spreads.","Sudden numbness or weakness on one side of the body, face drooping or trouble speaking is a stroke warning. Call emergency services."],['emsigns','vitamins']);
E('ear',"What should I do for ear pain or ringing in the ears?",['ear pain','earache','ear infection','blocked ear','ringing in ears','tinnitus','ear wax','ear discharge'],
 ["Ear pain is often from an infection or a blocked ear. Do not put anything in the ear, including buds or oil, unless a doctor says so."],
 ["Warmth on the outside of the ear and paracetamol can ease pain meanwhile.","See a doctor for severe pain, discharge, hearing loss or fever, and for any child with ear pain.","Ringing in the ears is often linked to loud noise. Lower headphone volume and see a doctor if it is in one ear or comes with sudden hearing loss."],['coldflu']);
E('fracture',"What should I do if I think a bone is broken?",['fracture','broken bone','bone broken','cracked bone','broke my arm','broke my leg'],
 ["Signs are severe pain, swelling, deformity and being unable to use the limb."],
 ["Keep the injured part still and support it in the position you found it. Do not try to straighten it.","Apply ice wrapped in cloth, and avoid food and drink in case it needs surgery.","Get urgent care. Call emergency services if the bone has pierced the skin, the limb is numb or blue, or the injury is to the head, neck or back."],['firstaid']);
E('uti',"What are the signs of a urine infection?",['uti','urine infection','burning urination','burning urine','painful urination','urinary infection','burning while peeing','frequent urination','peeing a lot'],
 ["A urine infection causes burning when you pass urine, a strong urge to go often, cloudy or smelly urine and lower stomach discomfort."],
 ["Drink more water and see a doctor, because antibiotics are usually needed.","Go sooner for fever, back pain, vomiting, blood in the urine, or if you are pregnant, a man or a child.","Frequent urination with a lot of thirst can also point to diabetes."],['kidney','diabetes']);
E('kidney',"What are kidney stones?",['kidney stone','kidney stones','kidney health','kidney pain','kidney problem','flank pain'],
 ["Kidney stones cause sudden, severe pain in the side or back that comes in waves, sometimes with nausea and blood in the urine."],
 ["Drinking enough water to pass about 2 to 2.5 litres of urine a day lowers the risk, unless your doctor limits fluids.","Go to a doctor. Get urgent help for fever, vomiting or being unable to pass urine."],['water','uti']);
E('sunburn',"How do I treat sunburn?",['sunburn','sun burn','sunburnt','tanning','sun protection','sunscreen use','sun tan'],
 ["Cool the skin with a cool compress or shower, apply aloe or a plain moisturiser, drink water and stay out of the sun."],
 ["Do not pop blisters. See a doctor for widespread blistering, fever or severe pain.","To prevent it, use SPF 30 or higher, reapply every two hours, wear a hat and avoid strong midday sun."],['skin','heat']);
E('hiccups',"How do I stop hiccups?",['hiccups','hiccup','hiccuping'],
 ["Most hiccups stop in minutes. Try holding your breath for 10 seconds, sipping cold water slowly or swallowing a spoon of sugar."],
 ["See a doctor if they last more than two days."],['acidity']);
E('nausea',"What helps with nausea or motion sickness?",['motion sickness','car sick','travel sickness','nausea','nauseous','feeling sick','queasy','travel nausea'],
 ["Look at the horizon, sit in the front or over the wing, get fresh air and avoid heavy meals before travel. Ginger can help."],
 ["Sip water or ORS slowly and eat bland food.","See a doctor for vomiting lasting more than a day, severe headache with stiff neck, or nausea in pregnancy that stops you keeping fluids down."],['diarrhea','water']);
E('sweat',"Why do I sweat so much?",['sweat','why do i sweat','body odor','body odour','excessive sweating','sweaty','hyperhidrosis','sweating a lot','night sweats','sweating at night'],
 ["Sweating is how the body cools down. Heat, exercise, stress, spicy food and caffeine all increase it."],
 ["Wash daily, wear breathable fabrics and use an antiperspirant.","See a doctor for sweating that suddenly increases, night sweats with fever or weight loss, or sweating with chest discomfort."],['thyroid','heat']);
E('bites',"What should I do after a dog or snake bite?",['snake bite','snakebite','dog bit','bitten by','bitten','dog bites','dog bite','rabies','animal bite','scorpion sting','stray dog','cat scratch','monkey bite'],
 ["Animal bite: wash the wound with soap and running water for 15 minutes, apply an antiseptic and go to a hospital for a rabies vaccine, even if the animal looked healthy."],
 ["Snake bite: keep the person calm and still, remove rings, keep the limb level with the heart and get to a hospital with antivenom at once.","Do not cut the wound, suck it, tie it tightly, or apply chilli, turmeric or ice.","Scorpion sting: wash, apply a cold pack and get medical help, especially for children."],['firstaid','emsigns']);
E('pcos',"What is PCOS?",['pcos','pcod','polycystic','pcos symptoms','hirsutism'],
 ["PCOS is a hormone condition. Signs include irregular periods, acne, extra facial or body hair, weight gain and trouble getting pregnant."],
 ["A doctor diagnoses it with blood tests and an ultrasound.","Weight loss of even 5 to 10%, regular exercise, a diet of whole foods and low in sugar, and good sleep can improve symptoms. Treatments are also available."],['menstrual','weightloss']);
E('sugar',"How much sugar is too much?",['sugar','sweets','sweet tooth','added sugar','sugar craving','sugar cravings','soft drink','soft drinks','cold drink','soda','cola','sweetener'],
 ["The WHO advises keeping added sugar below 10% of your calories, and ideally below 5%, which is about 25 g or 6 teaspoons a day."],
 ["The biggest sources are soft drinks, packaged juice, sweets and bakery items.","To cut cravings, sleep well, eat protein with meals and keep fruit at hand."],['diabetes','diet']);
E('salt',"How much salt should I eat?",['salt','how much salt','salt intake','daily salt','salt per day','less salt','sodium','too much salt','salty','low salt','pickle','processed food','namkeen','papad','instant noodles'],
 ["The WHO advises less than 5 g of salt a day, about one teaspoon. Most people eat much more."],
 ["Hidden salt is in pickles, papad, namkeen, chips, instant noodles, sauces and packaged food.","Taste before you add salt and use lemon, spices and herbs instead.","Too much salt raises blood pressure."],['bp','hearthealth']);
E('breakfast',"Should I skip breakfast or eat late at night?",['breakfast','skip breakfast','skipping meals','skip meal','meal timing','dinner time','late dinner','eat at night','late night eating','snack','snacks','snacking'],
 ["There is no single right answer. Eat when you are hungry and keep a regular pattern."],
 ["Try to finish dinner two to three hours before bed.","Good snacks are fruit, nuts, roasted chana, curd or sprouts.","Skipping meals then overeating tends to spike hunger and blood sugar."],['balanced','sleep']);
E('fruitveg',"How much fruit and vegetables should I eat?",['fruit','fruits','vegetables','veggies','fiber','fibre','salad','fruit juice','green leafy','how many vegetables'],
 ["Aim for about 400 g, or five portions, of fruit and vegetables a day, and 25 to 30 g of fibre."],
 ["Whole fruit is better than juice because it keeps the fibre.","Mix colours and add a leafy green daily."],['balanced','constipation']);
E('indianfood',"Is Indian food healthy?",['roti','rice','rice and diabetes','is rice bad','white rice','brown rice','dal','ghee','millet','millets','ragi','jowar','bajra','indian diet','indian food','chapati','paneer','curd','idli','dosa','biryani','sambar'],
 ["Traditional Indian meals can be very healthy. The key is balance and portion size."],
 ["Fill half the plate with vegetables, add dal or curd for protein and keep rice and roti to about a quarter each.","Try millets such as ragi, jowar and bajra for more fibre.","Use ghee and oil in small amounts, and go easy on fried snacks, refined flour and sweets."],['balanced','protein']);
E('herbs',"Do home remedies and herbs work?",['home remedy','home remedies','green tea','herbal tea','turmeric','haldi','ginger','tulsi','ayurveda','ayurvedic','kadha','giloy','amla','neem'],
 ["Some have modest evidence, such as ginger for nausea, honey for cough and turmeric as part of food. They support healthy habits but do not replace treatment."],
 ["Herbs and supplements can interact with medicines and some can harm the liver. Tell your doctor what you take.","Do not use them to treat a serious or lasting problem. See a doctor instead."],['vitamins','meds']);
E('eggsmeat',"Are eggs and meat healthy?",['egg','eggs','eat eggs','eggs daily','egg a day','eggs every day','egg yolk','red meat','chicken','vegetarian','vegan','non veg','mutton','fish','meat'],
 ["Eggs are a good protein source, and one a day is fine for most healthy people. Fish and chicken are healthy choices when not fried."],
 ["Limit red and processed meat.","Vegetarians can get protein from dal, paneer, curd, soy and sprouts. Vegans should take vitamin B12."],['protein','cholesterol']);
E('nuts',"How many nuts should I eat?",['nuts','how many nuts','how many almonds','almonds','walnuts','seeds','dry fruits','soaked almonds','peanuts','chia','flaxseed'],
 ["A small handful, about 30 g, a day is a good amount. Choose unsalted nuts."],
 ["Nuts are healthy but high in calories.","Walnuts, flaxseed and chia add omega-3 fats."],['diet','hearthealth']);
E('gymsupp',"Are gym supplements and fat burners safe?",['creatine','pre workout','gym supplement','gym supplements','anabolic steroids','bcaa','mass gainer','fat burner','fat burners','protein shake'],
 ["Creatine monohydrate is well studied and generally safe for healthy adults at about 3 to 5 g a day, with plenty of water."],
 ["Fat burners and pre-workouts often contain high doses of stimulants that raise heart rate and blood pressure. If you use them, you may see a higher pulse on PulseSpace.","Anabolic steroids can seriously harm the heart and liver.","Check with a doctor, choose tested products and be wary of big claims."],['protein','tachy']);
E('yoga',"Which yoga poses are good for beginners?",['yoga poses','start yoga','learn yoga','begin yoga','yoga for beginners','asana','asanas','surya namaskar','sun salutation','beginner yoga','yoga pose'],
 ["Good starter poses are mountain (tadasana), cat-cow, child's pose (balasana), cobra (bhujangasana), tree (vrikshasana) and downward dog."],
 ["Start with five rounds of surya namaskar at an easy pace, breathing naturally.","Move slowly and never push into pain. Learn from a qualified teacher if you have injuries, high blood pressure or are pregnant."],['mindful','stretching']);
E('warmup',"How should I warm up before exercise?",['warm up','warmup','warm up before exercise','dynamic stretching','before workout'],
 ["Spend five to ten minutes on light cardio, such as brisk walking, then do dynamic moves like arm circles, leg swings and bodyweight squats."],
 ["Finish with a five-minute slow cool down and gentle stretches."],['exercise','stretching']);
E('mealwalk',"Is it good to walk after meals?",['walk after meal','walking after meals','after dinner walk','post meal walk','walk after eating','walk after lunch'],
 ["Yes. A gentle 10 to 15 minute walk after meals helps lower blood sugar and can ease digestion."],
 ["Keep it easy. Hard exercise right after a big meal can cause cramps."],['steps','diabetes']);
E('hiit',"What is HIIT and is it safe?",['hiit','interval training','high intensity','tabata','circuit training'],
 ["HIIT alternates short hard efforts, such as 30 seconds, with easier recovery of 60 to 90 seconds."],
 ["Start with one or two sessions a week after you have a base of regular exercise.","Check with a doctor first if you have a heart condition, high blood pressure or chest symptoms.","Measure your resting HRV the next morning. A big drop means you need more rest."],['doms','exercise']);
E('sports',"Which sport or activity should I choose?",['cycling','swimming','swim','bicycle','dance','zumba','badminton','cricket','football','sports','which sport','which activity','best sport','best activity'],
 ["The best exercise is the one you enjoy enough to repeat. Walking, cycling, swimming, dancing and team sports all count."],
 ["Aim for 150 minutes a week of moderate activity and two strength sessions.","Swimming and cycling are easy on the joints."],['exercise','strength']);
E('sickworkout',"Should I exercise when I am sick?",['workout when sick','exercise when sick','exercise with cold','train when ill','exercise with fever','gym when sick'],
 ["Use the neck check. With symptoms only above the neck, such as a stuffy nose, light activity is usually fine."],
 ["With fever, body aches, chest congestion or a chesty cough, rest.","Ease back in gradually. A high resting pulse and low HRV on PulseSpace can show you are not recovered yet."],['illness','hrvgood']);
E('abs',"How do I get a flat stomach or abs?",['abs','six pack','core workout','plank','sit ups','crunches','core strength','flat stomach','belly workout'],
 ["You cannot burn fat from one area. Fat loss comes from your overall diet and activity, and abs show once body fat is low enough."],
 ["Strengthen the core with planks, bridges and dead bugs, three times a week.","Plank for 20 to 60 seconds and build up slowly."],['weightloss','strength']);
E('motivation',"How do I stay motivated to exercise?",['motivation','motivated','lazy','procrastinate','habit building','stay consistent','consistency','not in mood','no time to exercise'],
 ["Start tiny. Five minutes a day builds the habit and removes the excuse."],
 ["Do it at the same time each day and link it to something you already do.","Track your streak, or a morning PulseSpace reading, so you can see progress.","Find a partner or a sport you enjoy.","Expect resting heart rate and HRV to improve in four to eight weeks."],['routine','exercise']);
E('stretching',"How do I become more flexible?",['flexibility','flexible','become flexible','more flexible','stretching routine','tight hamstrings','touch toes','mobility','improve flexibility','stiff body'],
 ["Stretch for about ten minutes a day. Hold each stretch for 20 to 30 seconds without bouncing."],
 ["Stretch warm muscles, and stop at tension, not pain."],['yoga','posture']);
E('doms',"Why am I sore after a workout and do I need rest days?",['muscle soreness','doms','sore after workout','post workout','recovery day','rest day','overtraining','overtrained','muscles sore'],
 ["Soreness peaks 24 to 72 hours after unfamiliar exercise and is normal. Light movement, sleep, protein and water help."],
 ["Take one or two rest days a week.","Signs of overtraining are a high resting heart rate, low HRV, poor sleep and constant tiredness. PulseSpace can show the first two.","Sharp pain or joint pain is not normal soreness. Stop and rest."],['hrvgood','sleep']);
E('cramps',"What causes muscle cramps?",['muscle cramps','leg cramps','cramp','cramps','charley horse','night cramps'],
 ["Cramps often come from overuse, dehydration or low mineral levels, and some medicines can trigger them."],
 ["Stretch and gently massage the muscle, then drink water or an electrolyte drink.","See a doctor if cramps are frequent or severe, or if one calf is swollen, red or warm."],['water','doms']);
E('nap',"Is it good to nap, and why am I sleepy after lunch?",['nap','napping','power nap','afternoon sleepy','after lunch sleepy','post lunch','sleepy at work','afternoon slump'],
 ["A dip in energy after lunch is normal. A nap of 10 to 20 minutes, before 3 pm, can refresh you without ruining night sleep."],
 ["Eat a lighter lunch, drink water and take a short walk to beat the slump."],['insomnia','energy']);
E('nightmares',"What causes nightmares, sleepwalking or teeth grinding?",['nightmare','nightmares','sleep walking','sleepwalking','teeth grinding','bruxism','sleep paralysis','vivid dreams'],
 ["Stress, irregular sleep, alcohol and some medicines can trigger these. They are usually harmless."],
 ["Keep a regular sleep schedule and wind down before bed.","See a doctor if they happen often or cause injury. See a dentist for jaw pain or worn teeth.","Sleep paralysis is scary but harmless."],['sleep','stressmgmt']);
E('phone',"How do I cut down on phone and social media time?",['phone addiction','doomscrolling','social media','digital detox','phone before bed','blue light','too much phone','phone use'],
 ["Small rules work best: no phone for the hour before bed, charge it outside the bedroom and turn off non-essential notifications."],
 ["Set app limits and keep one screen-free meal a day.","Evening screens delay sleep mainly because they keep your mind busy."],['insomnia','eyes']);
E('longevity',"How can I live a longer, healthier life?",['longevity','live longer','longer life','healthier life','anti aging','ageing well','ageing','aging','stay young','healthy ageing'],
 ["The best-supported habits are regular activity, not smoking, good sleep, a mostly plant-based diet, strong social ties and regular check-ups."],
 ["Keep your muscles strong, because strength protects against falls.","Stay up to date on vaccines and screenings."],['hearthealth','strength']);
E('exams',"How do I handle exam stress?",['exam stress','exam','exams','study stress','study tips','study routine','board exam','revision','before exam','studying'],
 ["Plan your revision in 25 to 50 minute blocks with short breaks, and sleep properly. Sleep helps memory."],
 ["Avoid all-nighters, eat regular meals and move for ten minutes a day.","Try slow breathing before you start and before the exam.","If you feel overwhelmed, talk to someone you trust."],['breathtech','focus']);
E('anger',"How can I control anger or irritability?",['anger','angry','irritable','irritability','mood swings','frustrated','temper','short tempered'],
 ["Pause before you react. Breathe in for 4 and out for 6, and step away if you can."],
 ["Exercise releases tension. Poor sleep, hunger and stress all make irritability worse.","If anger is frequent or leads to harming others or yourself, speak to a counsellor."],['breathtech','stressmgmt']);
E('nerves',"How do I calm nerves before a presentation or interview?",['nervous','nervousness','stage fright','public speaking','social anxiety','shy','interview nerves','butterflies','presentation','interview'],
 ["Nerves and excitement feel the same in the body, so tell yourself you are excited. Rehearse out loud and arrive early."],
 ["Breathe in for 4 and out for 6 a few times before you start.","Skip extra caffeine. A faster pulse and shaky hands are normal and pass."],['breathtech','panic']);
E('workstress',"How do I deal with work stress and long hours?",['work stress','work from home','wfh','long hours','overworking','work life balance','office stress','deadline','boss','burnout'],
 ["Set clear start and end times, take a break every hour and walk at lunch."],
 ["Keep your desk and screen set up well and use the 20-20-20 eye rule.","If you feel exhausted, detached or less effective for weeks, that may be burnout. Talk to your manager or a doctor."],['posture','stressmgmt']);
E('journaling',"Does journaling or self-care help?",['journaling','gratitude','journal','self care','me time','hobby','hobbies'],
 ["Yes. Five minutes a day of writing down what went well, or what worries you, lowers stress for many people."],
 ["Time outdoors, hobbies and time with friends all help your mood and HRV."],['stressmgmt','mindful']);
E('spo2always',"Why is my SpO2 always 99 or 100?",['spo2 100','spo2 99','always 100','always 99','spo2 jumps','spo2 fluctuating','spo2 stuck','spo2 same'],
 ["99 to 100% is normal for a healthy person, and it is the top of the scale."],
 ["PulseSpace calculates SpO₂ from the red and infrared signal and limits it to 80 to 100%. It is uncalibrated, so it is best for noticing changes.","If it jumps by several points, your finger is probably moving or pressed too hard."],['spoacc','fingerpos']);
E('ledtune',"How do I adjust the sensor brightness or calibrate it?",['calibrate','calibration','led brightness','red light','infrared','sensor light','sensor hot','sensor gets hot','saturated','too bright'],
 ["The sketch sets LED brightness in the line sensor.setup(60, ...). The first number runs from 0 to 255."],
 ["If the signal is weak, raise it. If the wave looks flat-topped or clipped, lower it.","The sensor LEDs are always on while measuring, and a slightly warm sensor is normal.","Ambient light and finger pressure matter as much as brightness."],['trouble','fingerpos']);
E('zerobpm',"Why does it show dashes or 0 bpm?",['0 bpm','zero bpm','shows zero','showing zero','reads zero','sensor zero','dashes','no pulse detected','shows nothing','no readings','no reading','nothing shows','still dashes'],
 ["The sensor only reports a heart rate when it sees a finger and a steady beat. If the sketch sees no finger, you get dashes."],
 ["Rest a fingertip lightly on the window and keep still.","Check the wiring and that the sketch is running. The sketch sends W,0 when no finger is detected.","If it still fails, the finger threshold in the sketch may be too high for your sensor."],['trouble','fingerpos']);
E('hrjump',"Why does my heart rate jump around or show double?",['heart rate jumps','bpm jumps','bpm unstable','double reading','heart rate doubled','half reading','random bpm','bpm too high on sensor','unstable heart rate'],
 ["Finger sensors can count a second small bump in each pulse as an extra beat, or miss a beat. Movement does the same."],
 ["Keep your hand still on a table and press lightly.","PulseSpace ignores gaps outside 300 to 2000 ms and takes the median over the measurement, so the final value is steadier than the live one."],['variation','fingerpos']);
E('hrvmath',"How is HRV (RMSSD) calculated?",['how is hrv calculated','how is rmssd calculated','rmssd formula','hrv formula','sdnn','pnn50','rr interval','inter beat interval','beat interval','hrv metrics'],
 ["RMSSD is the square root of the average of the squared differences between successive beat-to-beat intervals. It reflects how much your heart rate varies from beat to beat."],
 ["PulseSpace removes beats more than 30% from the median interval and needs at least 8 clean beats.","Finger-sensor HRV is a good trend tool, but it is not identical to ECG-based HRV."],['hrvgood','stressscore']);
E('stressscore',"How is the stress score calculated?",['stress score calculated','calculate stress','stress calculation','how to measure stress','how is stress score','stress score formula','how stress score works','stress score meaning','stress score accuracy','stress number'],
 ["The 0 to 100 score blends two things: 65% from low HRV (RMSSD from 15 to 70 ms) and 35% from heart rate (60 to 110 bpm)."],
 ["Low HRV and a fast pulse raise it.","It estimates physical stress for fun and tracking. It is not a diagnosis."],['hrvgood','stressmgmt']);
E('baselines',"How do I track my progress over time?",['baseline','track trend','trend over time','track progress','compare days','weekly average','long term trend'],
 ["Press Save to journal after a measurement. The Journal tab then shows trends and 7-day averages. Measure at the same time each day."],
 ["Look at the 7-day average of resting heart rate and HRV rather than one reading.","A resting heart rate that falls and HRV that rises over weeks is a good sign."],['whenmeasure','privacy']);
E('power',"Can I power the sensor from 5V?",['5v','3 3v','voltage','power the sensor','level shifter','battery','power supply','power sensor','which voltage'],
 ["The MAX30102 chip runs on low voltage. Most breakout boards have a regulator, but check yours. Using 3.3 V on VIN is the safest."],
 ["Powering from the board's USB connection is fine.","Do not connect to a 5 V supply unless your board says it accepts it."],['wiring','hardware']);
E('upload',"How do I upload the sketch and install the library?",['arduino ide','upload sketch','upload','compile','compile error','library','sparkfun library','install library','heartrate h','max30105 h','board manager','baud rate','serial monitor'],
 ["In the Arduino IDE:"],
 ["Open Library Manager and install the SparkFun MAX3010x Pulse and Proximity Sensor Library.","Choose your board and port under Tools, open pulsespace.ino and press Upload.","If it says MAX30105.h not found, the library is missing.","Close the Serial Monitor afterwards. The baud rate is 115200."],['wiring','trouble']);
E('boards',"Which boards work with PulseSpace?",['which board','nodemcu','esp8266','raspberry pi','pico','teensy','board work','compatible board','compatible boards'],
 ["Any board with I2C and a USB serial connection works, such as the Uno, Nano, Mega, ESP32 and ESP8266."],
 ["ESP8266 typically uses SDA on D2 and SCL on D1.","A full Raspberry Pi needs different code. A Pico works through the Arduino core."],['wiring','hardware']);
E('wireless',"Can it work wirelessly?",['bluetooth','wifi','wireless','hc 05','hc05','ble','without usb','no cable','wireless sensor'],
 ["A Bluetooth serial module such as the HC-05, once paired in your computer's settings, can appear as a serial port that Chrome or Edge can open."],
 ["I have not tested this setup.","Direct Bluetooth Low Energy or WiFi would need changes to the sketch and the page."],['browser','boards']);

