E('readiness',"What is the readiness score?",['readiness','ready score','recovery score','how ready','readiness score'],
 ["Readiness is a single number from 0 to 100 that blends three things: HRV recovery (half the weight), resting heart rate and blood oxygen. Higher means your body looks more recovered."],
 ["Above 70 suggests a good day for activity.","40 to 70 is middling. Go easy and sleep well.","Below 40 suggests rest. It is a wellness estimate, not a diagnosis."],['hrvmath','whenmeasure']);
E('rhythmmap',"What is the heart-rhythm map?",['rhythm map','poincare','poincar','scatter plot','sd1','sd2','beat map'],
 ["Each dot plots one beat interval against the next. A tight round cloud along the diagonal means steady beats. A wider cloud means more variability, which is usually healthy at rest."],
 ["SD1 reflects beat-to-beat variability (linked to RMSSD).","SD2 reflects slower, longer-term variation.","Irregular, scattered dots with symptoms deserve a doctor visit."],['hrvmath']);
E('calmsession',"How does the calm session work?",['calm session','breathing session','guided breathing','calm mode','box breathing','4-7-8','sleep breathing'],
 ["Press Calm session on the results page. Pick a pattern and a length, then follow the circle: it grows as you breathe in and shrinks as you breathe out."],
 ["Relax is in for 4, out for 6.","Box is 4-4-4-4.","Sleep is 4-7-8.","Connect the sensor to watch your heart rate settle while you breathe."],['breathtech']);
E('journalhelp',"How do I save my readings?",['save to journal','save reading','journal','save my readings','keep history','readings history','delete journal','export csv'],
 ["After a measurement, add optional tags and a note, then press Save to journal. Open the Journal tab for averages, a trend chart and your saved entries."],
 ["Entries stay in this browser only.","Download a CSV from the Journal tab.","Clear the journal there too."],['privacy']);
E('insights',"What are baseline, streak and insights?",['baseline comparison','against my usual','streak','weekly goal','insights','pnn50','sdnn','beat regularity','copy summary'],
 ["After a few saved readings, the results page compares today with your usual, and the Journal shows a seven-day streak and which tags seem to move your numbers."],
 ["SDNN is the overall spread of your beat gaps. pNN50 is the share of beat-to-beat changes above 50 ms, a recovery marker.","Beat regularity is a simple steadiness check, not a rhythm diagnosis.","Copy summary puts your results on the clipboard to paste into a message."],['hrvmath','journalhelp']);
E('soundtheme',"Can I turn the heartbeat sound or light mode on?",['heartbeat sound','sound on','mute','light mode','dark mode','theme','sound off'],
 ["Use the speaker and sun/moon buttons at the top right. Sound plays a soft lub-dub with each detected beat during a measurement. Both choices are remembered on this device."],
 [],['journalhelp']);
