E('bpnormal',"What is a normal blood pressure?",['normal blood pressure','blood pressure normal','blood pressure range','blood pressure chart','blood pressure levels','what is normal bp','bp range','bp normal','high blood pressure','low blood pressure','hypertension symptoms','bp reading'],
 ["For most adults, a healthy blood pressure is below 120/80 mmHg. 120 to 129 over under 80 is slightly raised, 130/80 or more is high (stage 1), and 140/90 or more is stage 2."],
 ["High blood pressure usually has no symptoms, so measure it. Use an upper-arm cuff, seated and rested for five minutes.","180/120 or higher with chest pain, headache, vision change or confusion is an emergency.","PulseSpace cannot measure blood pressure. Type a reading like \"BP 128/82\" and I will interpret it."],['bplower','salt','bp']);
E('bplower',"What lowers blood pressure naturally?",['lower blood pressure','reduce blood pressure','foods lower blood pressure','foods for blood pressure','bring down bp','control blood pressure','lower bp naturally','bp control','dash diet','potassium'],
 ["Lifestyle changes can lower blood pressure by several points, sometimes as much as one tablet."],
 ["Cut salt to under 5 g a day and eat more fruit, vegetables, beans and low-fat dairy (the DASH pattern).","Walk briskly 30 minutes most days and lose extra weight.","Limit alcohol, stop smoking and manage stress.","Potassium-rich foods such as banana, coconut water, spinach and beans help, unless your doctor limits potassium.","Never stop blood pressure medicine without asking your doctor."],['salt','hearthealth']);
E('pots',"What is POTS or a fast heart rate on standing?",['pots','postural tachycardia','heart rate when standing','heart rate on standing','heart rate stand up','dizzy when standing','orthostatic','standing up dizzy','head rush','heart rate standing'],
 ["When you stand, blood pools in the legs and the heart speeds up by 10 to 20 beats to compensate. A jump of 30 or more beats within ten minutes of standing, with dizziness, may be POTS or dehydration."],
 ["Drink water, add a little salt if your doctor agrees, and rise slowly.","See a doctor if it happens often or you faint.","You can compare lying and standing heart rate with PulseSpace by measuring twice."],['dizzy','water']);
E('rhrchild',"What is a normal heart rate for babies and children?",['baby heart rate','child heart rate','infant heart rate','kids heart rate','toddler heart rate','heart rate for children','heart rate teenager','pediatric heart rate','newborn heart rate'],
 ["Children have faster hearts. Typical resting rates are about 100 to 160 for newborns, 80 to 130 for toddlers, 70 to 110 for school-age children and 60 to 100 for teenagers."],
 ["Fever, crying and play raise it.","PulseSpace is built for adults. Use a children's device and talk to a paediatrician for any worry."],['kids','rhr']);
E('agehr',"Does heart rate change with age?",['heart rate age','age and heart rate','older heart rate','heart rate older adults','heart rate in 60s','heart rate over 60','heart rate by age chart','age affect heart rate','heart rate 40 year old','heart rate 30 year old'],
 ["Resting heart rate stays about the same through adulthood, 60 to 100 for most people. Maximum heart rate and HRV both fall with age."],
 ["Estimated maximum heart rate is 220 minus your age.","Compare yourself with your own past readings more than with age charts."],['rhr','maxhr']);
E('fastingpulse',"What is resting heart rate and when should I measure it?",['resting pulse','fasting heart rate','heart rate on waking','morning heart rate','heart rate first thing','resting hr','true resting','lowest heart rate'],
 ["Resting heart rate is your pulse when calm and not recently active. The best time is in the morning before getting out of bed or having coffee."],
 ["Sit or lie quietly for five minutes first.","Check it on several mornings and use the average.","A resting rate that creeps up by 5 to 10 beats over days can be an early sign of stress, poor sleep or illness."],['whenmeasure','rhr']);
E('pulsemanual',"How do I check my pulse by hand?",['check pulse manually','take my pulse','count pulse','feel pulse','pulse by hand','measure pulse without','radial pulse','neck pulse','wrist pulse','find my pulse'],
 ["Place two fingers (not your thumb) on the inside of your wrist, below the thumb, or on the side of your neck. Press lightly until you feel the beat."],
 ["Count the beats for 30 seconds and multiply by 2, or for a full 60 seconds if the rhythm seems uneven.","Do not press hard on the neck, and never press both sides at once."],['rhr','palp']);
E('afib',"What is atrial fibrillation?",['atrial fibrillation','afib','a fib','irregularly irregular','racing irregular heartbeat','fibrillation'],
 ["Atrial fibrillation (AFib) is a common heart rhythm problem where the upper chambers beat chaotically. The pulse feels fast and irregular, and it raises the risk of stroke."],
 ["Symptoms: fluttering, breathlessness, tiredness, dizziness. Some people feel nothing.","An ECG diagnoses it. PulseSpace cannot.","See a doctor promptly for an irregular pulse that lasts, and get emergency help with chest pain or fainting."],['palp','emsigns']);
E('chesttight',"What causes chest tightness?",['chest tightness','tight chest','chest pressure','chest discomfort','chest heaviness','chest burning','pain in chest','chest hurts','heaviness in chest'],
 ["Chest tightness can come from muscle strain, acid reflux, anxiety or asthma, but it can also be a heart problem. Do not guess."],
 ["Call emergency services if it is crushing or spreads to the arm, jaw or back, or comes with sweating, breathlessness, nausea or fainting.","Seek care the same day for tightness with exercise that eases with rest.","Reflux and anxiety are common causes, yet only a doctor can say which."],['emsigns','acidity','panic']);
E('cyanosis',"Why do my lips or fingers look blue?",['blue lips','blue fingers','blue skin','fingers blue','lips blue','bluish','cyanosis','blue nails','purple fingers','pale fingers'],
 ["Blue or grey lips and tongue can mean low oxygen and need urgent medical care. Blue fingertips in the cold are often just poor circulation."],
 ["Blue lips, face or tongue, especially with breathlessness: call emergency services.","Fingers that go white then blue in the cold may be Raynaud's. Warm them and ask a doctor.","A cold fingertip also lowers PulseSpace readings."],['lowspo2','coldhands']);
E('hearthealthnum',"What health checks should I get?",['health checkup','health check','annual checkup','blood tests','screening','master health check','what tests','routine tests','full body checkup','which tests'],
 ["A sensible yearly check for most adults covers blood pressure, weight, blood sugar, cholesterol and a general review. Add tests for your age and family history."],
 ["From about 30 to 40, check blood sugar and cholesterol regularly.","Women: ask about cervical and breast screening. Men over 50: ask about prostate advice.","Over 45 or with family history: ask about colon screening."],['bp','diabetes','cholesterol']);
E('coldself',"I have a cold. What should I do?",['i have a cold','got a cold','catching a cold','cold symptoms','head cold','cold remedy','cold remedies','treat cold','cold home remedy','cold cure','cold medicine'],
 ["A common cold passes in 7 to 10 days. Rest, fluids and simple comfort measures are the main treatment."],
 ["Drink warm fluids, gargle with warm salt water and use steam or a saline spray.","Paracetamol can ease aches and fever. Antibiotics do not work on colds.","See a doctor for breathlessness, chest pain, fever over three days, or symptoms that get worse after a week."],['coldflu','fevercare','cough']);
E('sorethroat',"How do I treat a sore throat?",['sore throat','throat pain','throat infection','strep','tonsil','tonsillitis','scratchy throat','pain swallowing','hoarse voice','lost voice'],
 ["Most sore throats are viral and settle in a few days. Warm fluids, honey, lozenges and gargling warm salt water help."],
 ["See a doctor for trouble swallowing or breathing, drooling, a very high fever, white patches, or a sore throat longer than a week.","Rest your voice if it is hoarse."],['coldflu','cough']);
E('lowfever',"What temperature is a fever?",['what is fever','normal body temperature','temperature fever','thermometer reading','98.6','37 degrees','100.4','fever range','low grade fever','is 99 a fever'],
 ["Normal body temperature is about 36.1 to 37.2 °C (97 to 99 °F). A fever is 38 °C (100.4 °F) or higher. Type a number like \"101 F in C\" and I will convert it."],
 ["Measure with a digital thermometer, not the PulseSpace sensor.","See a doctor for fever lasting over three days, or sooner in babies, older adults and people with long-term illness."],['fevercare','bodytemp']);
E('lowbloodsugar',"What should I do about shakiness and sweating from low sugar?",['low sugar','shaky hands','shaking','trembling','sugar drop','hungry shaky','sweaty and shaky','blood sugar drop','hypoglycemia symptoms'],
 ["Shakiness, sweating, hunger and a pounding heart can be low blood sugar. If you can swallow, take about 15 g of fast sugar such as juice, glucose tablets or sugar in water."],
 ["Recheck after 15 minutes and eat something with starch if you feel better.","If you feel confused or cannot swallow, someone should call emergency services.","Frequent episodes need a doctor."],['diabetes','palp']);
E('prediabetes',"How do I prevent diabetes?",['prevent diabetes','prediabetes','pre diabetes','diabetes risk','reduce diabetes risk','family history diabetes','diabetes prevention','insulin resistance','hba1c','a1c'],
 ["Prediabetes means blood sugar is higher than normal but not yet diabetes. It can often be reversed."],
 ["Losing 5 to 7% of body weight and walking 150 minutes a week cuts risk by more than half.","Eat more fibre, fewer sugary drinks and refined carbs.","An HbA1c of 5.7 to 6.4% is prediabetes and 6.5% or more suggests diabetes. Ask your doctor to test you."],['diabetes','sugar','exercise']);
E('hba1c',"What are normal blood sugar levels?",['normal blood sugar','fasting sugar','fasting blood sugar','sugar range','post meal sugar','random sugar','glucose range','sugar 100','sugar 140','blood glucose normal'],
 ["Typical fasting blood sugar is under 100 mg/dL (5.6 mmol/L). 100 to 125 is prediabetes range and 126 or more on two tests suggests diabetes. Two hours after a meal it should stay under 140."],
 ["Only a lab test or glucometer measures this. PulseSpace cannot.","Your doctor sets your own targets."],['diabetes','prediabetes']);
E('cholnumbers',"What are healthy cholesterol numbers?",['cholesterol numbers','ldl level','hdl level','cholesterol range','good cholesterol','bad cholesterol','lower cholesterol','reduce cholesterol','high cholesterol','statin','cholesterol 200'],
 ["For most adults: total cholesterol under 200 mg/dL, LDL under 100, HDL above 40 for men and 50 for women, triglycerides under 150. People at higher risk need lower LDL targets."],
 ["Eat more oats, beans, nuts, fruit and fish, and fewer fried and processed foods.","Exercise and weight loss raise HDL and lower LDL.","Your doctor decides on tablets such as statins."],['cholesterol','hearthealth','diet']);
E('stroke',"How can I lower my stroke risk?",['stroke risk','prevent stroke','after stroke','mini stroke','tia','stroke prevention','brain stroke'],
 ["Most strokes are preventable. The big levers are blood pressure, not smoking, activity, healthy weight and treating AFib and diabetes."],
 ["Know the FAST signs and call emergency services at once.","A brief episode of weakness or speech trouble that passes (a TIA) still needs urgent care."],['emsigns','bplower','afib']);
E('anxietysym',"What does anxiety feel like in the body?",['anxiety symptoms','anxiety attack','anxious heartbeat','nervous stomach','worry','anxiety heart','anxiety chest','feeling anxious','always anxious','anxiety disorder','overthinking'],
 ["Anxiety can cause a pounding heart, fast breathing, sweating, tight chest, shaky hands, nausea and a sense of dread. It is common and treatable."],
 ["Slow breathing, a walk and cutting caffeine help in the moment.","Talk to a doctor or counsellor if worry is frequent or limits your life. Therapy works well.","Do not ignore chest pain by assuming anxiety. Get it checked once."],['panic','breathtech','stressmgmt']);
E('depression',"What are signs of depression?",['depression symptoms','signs of depression','feel empty','no interest','lost interest','feeling down','always sad','low mood weeks','mental health help','therapy','counselling','counseling'],
 ["Depression means low mood or loss of interest lasting two weeks or more, often with poor sleep, appetite changes, tiredness and trouble concentrating."],
 ["Talk to a doctor or counsellor. It is a medical condition and treatable.","Daily sunlight, movement, routine and time with people help alongside treatment.","If you think of harming yourself, contact emergency services or a crisis line now."],['lowmood','stressmgmt']);
E('burnoutsigns',"How do I know if I am burned out?",['burned out','burnt out','exhausted at work','dread work','cynical','emotionally drained','drained','no motivation work'],
 ["Burnout is long-term exhaustion from stress, often with cynicism and feeling ineffective."],
 ["Rest, set boundaries, take real days off and talk to your manager.","A high resting heart rate and low HRV for weeks can show strain.","See a doctor if you cannot cope or feel hopeless."],['workstress','hrvgood']);
E('sleephours',"How many hours of sleep do I need?",['how many hours sleep','hours of sleep','sleep duration','how much sleep','sleep requirement','enough sleep','sleep hours','sleep needs','oversleeping','too much sleep','sleep 6 hours'],
 ["Most adults need 7 to 9 hours. Teenagers need 8 to 10, and older adults 7 to 8."],
 ["Regular timing matters as much as length.","Sleeping much more than 9 hours every day can also point to a health issue.","Poor sleep raises resting heart rate and lowers HRV."],['sleep','insomnia']);
E('sleephygiene',"How can I sleep better tonight?",['sleep better','better sleep','sleep tips','improve sleep','sleep hygiene','good sleep','sleep routine','deep sleep','sleep quality','sleep schedule','rest well'],
 ["Good sleep is mostly habits."],
 ["Same bed and wake time daily, even on weekends.","Dim lights and put screens away an hour before bed.","Keep the room cool, dark and quiet.","No caffeine after noon, and avoid alcohol and large meals near bedtime.","If you cannot sleep after 20 minutes, get up and do something calm."],['insomnia','nap']);
E('snoringfix',"How do I stop snoring?",['stop snoring','snoring remedy','loud snoring','snoring partner','sleep on side','snoring cure'],
 ["Snoring is often helped by sleeping on your side, losing weight, avoiding alcohol at night and treating a blocked nose."],
 ["Loud snoring with gasping, pauses in breathing or heavy daytime sleepiness may be sleep apnea. See a doctor."],['apnea','sleep']);
E('weightlossplan',"How can I lose weight at home?",['lose weight at home','weight loss at home','home workout','how to lose 5 kg','lose 10 kg','weight loss tips','lose weight fast','slim down','fat burning','burn calories','lose belly','diet to lose weight','weight loss diet'],
 ["Steady weight loss comes from a calorie deficit you can keep, mostly through food choices plus daily movement."],
 ["Aim for 0.25 to 0.5 kg a week. Faster is usually muscle and water.","Walk 8,000 to 10,000 steps, add 2 or 3 short strength sessions of squats, push-ups and planks.","Fill half the plate with vegetables, eat protein at every meal and cut sugary drinks.","Sleep 7 or more hours. Short sleep increases hunger."],['weightloss','steps','strength']);
E('gainweight',"How can I gain weight healthily?",['gain weight healthy','underweight','too thin','how to gain weight','weight gain diet','build mass','bulking'],
 ["Add calories with nutritious food and lift weights so the gain is muscle."],
 ["Eat three meals and two or three snacks such as nuts, banana with peanut butter, milk, eggs or paneer.","Strength train three times a week.","See a doctor if you lose weight without trying."],['protein','strength']);
E('hydrationsign',"How do I know if I am dehydrated?",['signs of dehydration','dehydration symptoms','dark urine','dry mouth','thirsty','urine colour','urine color','not drinking enough water','dehydrated heart rate'],
 ["Dark urine, thirst, dry mouth, headache, tiredness and dizziness are signs. Dehydration raises heart rate and lowers HRV."],
 ["Aim for pale yellow urine.","Use ORS for vomiting, diarrhoea or heavy sweating.","Seek care for confusion, no urine for 8 hours or fainting."],['water','tachy']);
E('electrolytes',"Do I need electrolytes or coconut water?",['electrolytes','sports drink','coconut water','oral rehydration','salt water drink','nimbu pani','lemon water','buttermilk','sugarcane juice'],
 ["For normal days, water is enough. Electrolyte drinks help after heavy sweating, long exercise, heat or stomach illness."],
 ["Coconut water, nimbu pani with a pinch of salt and buttermilk are good home options.","People with kidney disease or high blood pressure should ask a doctor."],['water','heat']);
E('breakfastfoods',"What is a healthy breakfast?",['healthy breakfast','breakfast ideas','what to eat in morning','morning food','oats','poha','upma','eggs for breakfast','breakfast protein','idli healthy'],
 ["A good breakfast combines protein, fibre and a little healthy fat so energy stays steady."],
 ["Examples: eggs with whole-grain toast, oats with nuts and fruit, vegetable poha or upma with curd, idli with sambar, sprouts chaat.","Limit sugary cereals, pastries and fruit juice."],['balanced','protein']);
E('snackideas',"What are healthy snacks?",['healthy snack','snack ideas','evening snack','what to snack','roasted chana','makhana','sprouts','fruit snack','snacks for weight loss','junk food craving','chips craving'],
 ["Pick snacks with protein or fibre: they keep you full longer."],
 ["Roasted chana, makhana, sprouts, fruit with a few nuts, curd, boiled egg, vegetable sticks with hummus.","Keep sweets and chips out of sight rather than relying on willpower."],['breakfast','sugar']);
E('energyfood',"What should I eat for energy?",['food for energy','energy foods','what to eat for energy','tired eat','low energy food','boost stamina','pre workout meal','before exercise eat','eat before workout','after workout food','post workout meal'],
 ["Steady energy comes from slow carbohydrates, protein and healthy fat, plus water."],
 ["Before exercise: a banana or oats about an hour earlier.","After exercise: protein plus carbs, for example eggs and toast, dal and rice, curd and fruit.","Avoid long gaps between meals."],['protein','energy']);
E('cutsalt',"How do I eat less salt?",['reduce salt','cut salt','less salt','salt substitute','low sodium','salt blood pressure','hidden salt'],
 ["Most salt comes from packaged and restaurant food, not the shaker."],
 ["Check labels for sodium. Over 600 mg per 100 g is high.","Cook from scratch, use lemon, garlic, pepper and herbs.","Reduce pickles, papad, chips, instant noodles and sauces."],['salt','bplower']);
E('transfat',"Are fried foods and ghee bad for the heart?",['fried food','trans fat','saturated fat','cooking oil','ghee heart','coconut oil','olive oil','mustard oil','refined oil','deep fried','vanaspati'],
 ["The type and amount of fat matter. Trans fats and a lot of saturated fat raise LDL cholesterol."],
 ["Avoid vanaspati and packaged bakery items with partially hydrogenated oil.","Use oil and ghee in small amounts. Mustard, groundnut, olive and rice bran oil are reasonable choices.","Replace some fried food with grilled, steamed or baked."],['cholnumbers','diet']);
E('fibregut',"How do I keep my gut healthy?",['gut health','probiotic','probiotics','curd gut','digestion','bloating','gas problem','stomach gas','flatulence','fibre gut','prebiotic','indigestion remedy','digestive','bowel'],
 ["A healthy gut likes fibre, variety, fluids and regular meals."],
 ["Eat vegetables, fruit, legumes and whole grains. Curd and buttermilk add friendly bacteria.","Eat slowly and walk after meals.","See a doctor for blood in stool, weight loss, night pain or changes lasting more than three weeks."],['constipation','acidity','mealwalk']);
E('lactose',"Why does milk upset my stomach?",['lactose','lactose intolerance','milk allergy','dairy','milk bloating','cannot digest milk','gluten','celiac','food intolerance','food allergy','wheat allergy'],
 ["Lactose intolerance causes bloating, gas and loose stools after dairy because of low lactase. It is common and not dangerous."],
 ["Try curd, paneer, lactose-free milk or smaller portions.","Gluten problems (celiac disease) and food allergies are different. Swelling, hives or wheeze after eating need urgent care.","Get tested rather than cutting out foods long-term."],['allergy','fibregut']);
E('anemiadiet',"What should I eat if I have low haemoglobin?",['low hemoglobin food','increase hemoglobin','iron rich food','iron foods','hemoglobin diet','raise haemoglobin','beetroot','jaggery','dates iron','spinach iron','ferritin'],
 ["Iron is found in lentils, chickpeas, spinach, jaggery, dates, pumpkin seeds, eggs and meat. Pair it with vitamin C such as lemon or amla."],
 ["Tea and coffee with meals reduce iron absorption, so have them between meals.","A blood test and a doctor should confirm anaemia. Do not take iron tablets blindly."],['anemia','vitamins']);
E('vitd',"How do I get enough vitamin D?",['vitamin d','vitamin d deficiency','vitamin d sunlight','sun exposure','vitamin d symptoms','low vitamin d','d3','sunlight','bone pain vitamin'],
 ["Sunlight on bare skin for 15 to 30 minutes a few times a week helps, and some foods like eggs, fish and fortified milk add a little."],
 ["Low levels cause tiredness and bone or muscle aches. A blood test confirms it.","Supplements are common but ask your doctor for the dose."],['vitamins','osteo']);
E('b12',"What are signs of low vitamin B12?",['b12 deficiency','vitamin b12','b12 symptoms','tingling feet','b12 foods','vegetarian b12','low b12'],
 ["Low B12 can cause tiredness, tingling in hands and feet, memory trouble, a sore tongue and anaemia. It is common in vegetarians and vegans."],
 ["Sources: eggs, dairy, fish, meat and fortified foods.","A blood test checks it, and a doctor can advise tablets or injections."],['vitamins','numbness']);
E('stressfoods',"Which foods help with stress?",['food for stress','stress eating','comfort eating','emotional eating','stress and appetite','anxiety diet','calming foods','magnesium food','mood food'],
 ["No food cures stress, but regular meals and nutrients like magnesium, omega-3 and fibre support mood."],
 ["Try nuts, seeds, leafy greens, bananas, oats, curd and fish.","Limit sugar and heavy caffeine, which can worsen jitters.","If you eat to cope, a short walk or breathing first can break the habit."],['stressmgmt','nuts']);
E('smokingquit',"How do I quit smoking?",['quit smoking','stop smoking','give up cigarettes','smoking cessation','nicotine patch','quit tobacco','chewing tobacco','gutka','hookah','cigarette craving'],
 ["Quitting is the best thing you can do for your heart. Many people need several attempts."],
 ["Set a quit date, tell people and remove cigarettes.","Cravings pass in about 10 minutes. Walk, drink water or breathe slowly.","Ask a doctor about nicotine replacement or medicines, and call a quit-line.","Your heart rate and oxygen improve within days to weeks."],['smoking','hearthealth']);
E('alcoholcut',"How much alcohol is safe?",['safe alcohol','how much alcohol','drinking limit','alcohol units','binge drinking','quit alcohol','stop drinking','alcohol heart','alcohol every day','alcohol liver'],
 ["There is no completely safe level. Lower is better. Many guidelines say no more than 1 drink a day for women and 2 for men, with alcohol-free days."],
 ["Alcohol raises resting heart rate and lowers HRV for a night or more.","If you cannot cut down, or need a drink to start the day, talk to a doctor. Stopping suddenly after heavy use can be dangerous."],['alcohol','jaundice']);
E('beginnerwalk',"How do I start a walking habit?",['start walking','walking routine','walking plan','brisk walk','walk for health','how long to walk','walking weight loss','walking benefits','benefits of walking','walking daily'],
 ["Walking is the easiest exercise to keep. It lowers blood pressure, blood sugar, stress and resting heart rate."],
 ["Start with 10 to 15 minutes and add 5 minutes each week up to 30 to 45.","A brisk pace lets you talk but not sing.","Link it to a habit, such as after dinner."],['steps','exercise','mealwalk']);
E('hometraining',"What is a simple home workout?",['home workout','workout at home','no gym workout','bodyweight workout','exercise without gym','workout routine','beginner workout','exercise plan','workout plan','full body workout','squats'],
 ["A short bodyweight routine three times a week is enough to start."],
 ["Warm up 5 minutes. Then do 2 or 3 rounds of: 10 squats, 8 push-ups (on knees if needed), 10 lunges, a 20-second plank, 10 glute bridges.","Rest a day between sessions and cool down with stretches.","Stop if you feel chest pain, dizziness or sharp pain."],['strength','warmup','exercise']);
E('cardioheart',"How do I train my heart?",['improve cardio','cardio fitness','improve stamina','endurance','build stamina','heart fitness','improve fitness','get fit','become fit','how to be fit','aerobic','zone 2'],
 ["Regular aerobic exercise strengthens the heart so it pumps more per beat. Your resting heart rate falls and HRV rises."],
 ["Do about 150 minutes a week of brisk walking, cycling, swimming or jogging at a pace where you can still talk.","Add one short harder session a week as you progress.","Measure resting heart rate monthly to see your progress."],['exercise','rhr','vo2']);
E('hrafterfood',"Why does my heart rate go up after eating?",['heart rate after eating','heart rate after meal','pulse after food','fast heartbeat after eating','palpitations after meal','heart rate after coffee','after dinner heart'],
 ["Digestion needs extra blood flow, so heart rate often rises by 5 to 10 beats after a large meal. Sugar, caffeine and alcohol add to it."],
 ["Measure before eating or wait two hours.","See a doctor if you get strong palpitations, dizziness or chest discomfort after meals."],['whenmeasure','caffeine']);
E('hrhot',"Does hot or cold weather change my heart rate?",['hot weather heart rate','cold weather heart','heart rate summer','heart rate winter','heat heart rate','sauna','hot bath','cold shower','ice bath','steam bath'],
 ["Heat makes the heart beat faster to cool the body. Cold narrows blood vessels and can raise blood pressure."],
 ["Drink more in hot weather.","Avoid very hot baths or saunas if you have heart disease or low blood pressure.","Cold fingers weaken the PulseSpace signal."],['heat','coldhands']);
E('hrfever',"Why is my heart rate high with a fever?",['heart rate fever','pulse fever','fever fast heartbeat','fever tachycardia','sick heart rate','heart rate illness','heart rate infection'],
 ["Each degree Celsius of fever raises heart rate by about 8 to 10 beats per minute, because your metabolism speeds up."],
 ["Rest, drink fluids and treat the fever.","See a doctor if your pulse stays above 120 at rest or you feel breathless."],['fevercare','illness']);
E('hrmedsraise',"Which things raise my heart rate?",['what raises heart rate','heart rate increases','causes of high pulse','why heart rate rises','heart rate trigger','things that raise heart rate','heart rate up'],
 ["Common triggers: caffeine, nicotine, stress, anxiety, dehydration, fever, anaemia, thyroid problems, poor sleep, alcohol, standing up, heat and some medicines."],
 ["Look at what changed recently.","If your resting pulse is over 100 for days without a clear cause, see a doctor."],['tachy','caffeine','thyroid']);
E('hrlowers',"What lowers my heart rate?",['lower resting heart rate','reduce heart rate','bring heart rate down','slow heart rate naturally','decrease pulse','how to lower pulse','calm heart rate','settle heart','heart rate down'],
 ["Regular exercise, good sleep, slow breathing, hydration and less caffeine all lower resting heart rate over time."],
 ["In the moment: sit, breathe in for 4 and out for 6, and drink water.","Do not use medicines to slow the pulse unless a doctor prescribes them."],['breathtech','exercise','tachy']);
E('hrvimprove',"How can I improve my HRV?",['improve hrv','increase hrv','raise hrv','boost hrv','hrv low how to','better hrv','hrv improve','hrv tips','hrv training'],
 ["HRV improves slowly with habits that help recovery."],
 ["Sleep 7 to 9 hours on a regular schedule.","Exercise most days, but include rest days.","Slow breathing for 5 minutes daily.","Limit alcohol and late caffeine.","Measure at the same time each morning and watch the 7-day average."],['hrvgood','breathtech','sleep']);
E('hrvmorning',"Why is my HRV different every morning?",['hrv changes','hrv fluctuates','hrv varies','hrv daily','hrv inconsistent','hrv up and down','hrv dropped','hrv day to day'],
 ["HRV swings a lot from day to day with sleep, stress, food, training and measurement conditions. One low number is not a problem."],
 ["Look at the 7-day average.","A drop lasting several days points to strain or illness."],['hrvgood','variation']);
E('stressheart',"How does stress affect the heart?",['stress and heart','stress heart rate','stress effect on heart','chronic stress','stress blood pressure','stress heart disease','does stress affect heart','stress hormones','cortisol','adrenaline','fight or flight'],
 ["Stress releases adrenaline and cortisol, which raise heart rate and blood pressure. Short bursts are normal. Long-term stress adds to heart disease risk."],
 ["Regular exercise, sleep, social contact and slow breathing reduce the effect.","Use the Calm session in PulseSpace and watch your heart rate settle."],['stressmgmt','breathtech']);
E('coffeecup',"Is coffee bad for my heart?",['coffee bad for heart','coffee heart','is coffee bad','how much coffee','coffee palpitations','coffee anxiety','decaf','coffee and blood pressure','tea heart','green tea heart'],
 ["For most healthy adults, up to about 3 to 4 cups of coffee a day is fine and may even be protective. It can raise heart rate and blood pressure for a few hours."],
 ["If coffee causes palpitations, anxiety or poor sleep, cut back.","Avoid caffeine in the afternoon.","Sweet coffee drinks add a lot of sugar."],['caffeine','sleep']);
E('chestmuscle',"How can I tell muscle chest pain from heart pain?",['muscle chest pain','rib pain','chest wall pain','pain when pressing chest','costochondritis','pain on deep breath','sharp chest pain','stitch','side pain'],
 ["Pain that is sharp, worse when you press the area, twist or breathe deeply is more often from muscles or ribs. Heart pain is usually pressure or heaviness and may spread."],
 ["You cannot be sure at home. If in doubt, or with sweating, breathlessness or pain spreading to the arm or jaw, get emergency help.","See a doctor for pain that lasts days."],['chesttight','emsigns']);
E('pregnancyheart',"Which readings matter in pregnancy?",['pregnancy heart rate','pregnant oxygen','pregnant palpitations','pregnancy spo2','pregnancy exercise','pregnancy blood pressure','pregnancy dizziness','pregnant fast pulse','trimester heart'],
 ["Heart rate rises 10 to 20 beats in pregnancy and blood volume increases by about half. Oxygen should stay at 95% or higher."],
 ["Report headaches, vision changes, swelling or high blood pressure to your doctor quickly.","Walking and gentle exercise are usually good, with your doctor's approval."],['pregnancy','bp']);
E('menopausehr',"Why do I get palpitations around menopause?",['menopause palpitations','hot flush','hot flashes','perimenopause','menopause heart','hormone heart','estrogen heart','night sweats menopause'],
 ["Falling oestrogen can cause hot flushes, night sweats and a pounding heart. It is common and usually harmless."],
 ["Cut caffeine and alcohol, stay cool and exercise.","See a doctor for frequent or long palpitations, chest pain or fainting. Heart risk rises after menopause."],['menstrual','palp']);
E('mensperiod',"What helps period pain?",['period pain','menstrual cramps','cramps period','dysmenorrhea','heavy periods','pms symptoms','pain during periods','period relief','irregular period','missed period','late period'],
 ["Heat, gentle exercise and over-the-counter pain relief taken as the label says help most period pain."],
 ["See a doctor for pain that stops daily life, very heavy bleeding (soaking a pad every hour), or periods that stop or become irregular.","A missed period can be pregnancy, stress, thyroid or PCOS."],['menstrual','pcos']);
E('eldercare',"How can older adults stay healthy?",['elderly health','old age health','senior health','grandparents health','aging health','seniors','older people','elder care','parent health','falls elderly','fall prevention'],
 ["For older adults the biggest wins are staying active, preventing falls, eating enough protein, and keeping up with checks and vaccines."],
 ["Walk daily and add balance and strength exercises.","Review medicines yearly with a doctor.","Drink fluids even when not thirsty.","PulseSpace ranges are for adults. Compare an older person's readings with their own usual."],['longevity','strength']);
E('teenhealth',"What should teenagers know about health?",['teenager health','teen health','adolescent','puberty','growth','school child health','student health','college health','exam sleep'],
 ["Teenagers need 8 to 10 hours of sleep, regular activity and balanced meals. Heart rates run a little higher than adults'."],
 ["Limit energy drinks and screen time before bed.","Talk to a doctor or counsellor about low mood, anxiety or eating worries."],['sleep','exams']);
E('covidlong',"What is long COVID?",['long covid','post covid','after covid','covid recovery','covid tiredness','covid heart rate','covid palpitations','covid oxygen','post viral'],
 ["Some people have tiredness, breathlessness, brain fog and a fast heart rate for weeks after an infection."],
 ["Rest, pace yourself and return to activity gradually.","A higher resting pulse and lower HRV can show you are still recovering.","See a doctor if symptoms last more than a month or get worse."],['covid','fatigue']);
E('fluvsC',"How do I tell flu from a cold?",['flu or cold','flu vs cold','difference between cold and flu','flu symptoms','influenza symptoms','body ache fever cough','viral fever','seasonal flu','h1n1','swine flu'],
 ["Flu hits suddenly with high fever, body aches and tiredness. A cold is milder and starts with a stuffy or runny nose."],
 ["Rest, fluids and paracetamol help. A doctor may give antivirals if started early.","Get urgent care for breathlessness, chest pain, confusion or fever in a baby or older adult."],['coldflu','fevercare']);
E('tbsigns',"What are the signs of tuberculosis?",['tuberculosis','tb','tb symptoms','cough with blood','blood in sputum','long cough weight loss','night sweats cough','tb test'],
 ["A cough lasting more than two to three weeks, with fever, night sweats, weight loss or blood in the sputum, needs a TB test."],
 ["TB is curable with a full course of medicines.","See a doctor promptly and avoid close contact with others until checked."],['cough','sweat']);
E('worms',"Do I need to worry about stomach worms or infections?",['worms','deworming','stomach worms','parasite','giardia','amoeba','loose stools weeks','stomach infection','h pylori','ulcer','stomach ulcer'],
 ["Contaminated food or water can cause worms and gut infections. Wash hands, drink clean water and cook food well."],
 ["See a doctor for long-lasting loose stools, stomach pain, weight loss or black stools.","Ulcers cause burning pain between meals and need treatment."],['diarrhea','acidity']);
E('uticare',"How can I prevent urine infections?",['prevent uti','recurrent uti','urinary infection prevention','drink water uti','urine burning','cystitis','bladder infection','urine smell','blood in urine'],
 ["Drink plenty of water, pass urine when you need to and after sex, and wipe front to back."],
 ["Blood in urine always needs a doctor.","Fever or back pain with urinary symptoms means see a doctor the same day."],['uti','kidney']);
E('kidneyhealth',"How do I protect my kidneys?",['protect kidneys','kidney disease','kidney failure','creatinine','kidney function','swollen feet kidney','foamy urine','painkiller kidney','kidney tests'],
 ["Control blood pressure and sugar, drink enough water, avoid regular painkillers like ibuprofen unless advised, and limit salt."],
 ["Swelling in feet or face, foamy urine and tiredness deserve a test.","Creatinine and urine tests check kidney function."],['bp','diabetes','kidney']);
E('thyroidsigns',"What are signs of thyroid problems?",['thyroid symptoms','hypothyroid','hyperthyroid','thyroid test','thyroid weight','neck swelling','goitre','goiter','thyroid hair','cold intolerance','heat intolerance'],
 ["Underactive thyroid: tiredness, weight gain, feeling cold, dry skin, slow pulse. Overactive: weight loss, sweating, anxiety, fast pulse."],
 ["A TSH blood test checks it, and treatment is simple.","See a doctor for a lump in the neck."],['thyroid','tachy','fatigue']);
E('eyecare',"How do I look after my eyes?",['eye care','eyesight tips','eye exercise','glasses','screen eyes','eye drops','eye redness','pink eye','conjunctivitis','styes','vision test'],
 ["Rest your eyes with the 20-20-20 rule, use good light and get an eye test every one to two years."],
 ["Pink eye with discharge is infectious. Wash hands and see a doctor.","Sudden vision loss, flashes or severe pain need urgent care."],['eyes','phone']);
E('hearing',"How do I protect my hearing?",['hearing loss','protect hearing','headphones volume','loud music','earphones','hearing test','ear protection','deaf'],
 ["Keep headphone volume below about 60% and take breaks. Loud noise damages hearing for life."],
 ["Ringing or muffled hearing after a loud event should be checked.","Sudden hearing loss in one ear is urgent."],['ear']);
E('oralhealth',"How do I prevent cavities and gum disease?",['cavities','gum disease','bleeding gums','tooth decay','floss','mouthwash','oral hygiene','brush teeth','dental care','sensitive teeth','wisdom tooth'],
 ["Brush twice a day with fluoride toothpaste, floss daily and cut back on sugary snacks."],
 ["Gum disease is linked with heart disease, so look after your gums.","Visit a dentist twice a year, sooner for pain or swelling."],['dental']);
E('skinsun',"How do I protect my skin from the sun?",['skin cancer','mole','moles','sun damage','spf','sunscreen daily','tan removal','pigmentation','dark spots','dark circles','wrinkles'],
 ["Use SPF 30 or higher on exposed skin daily, reapply every two hours outdoors, and wear a hat in strong sun."],
 ["See a doctor for a mole that changes in size, colour or shape, or a sore that does not heal.","Dark circles are usually from sleep, genetics and allergies."],['sunburn','skin']);
E('acnecare',"How can I treat acne?",['acne treatment','pimple','pimples remedy','oily skin','blackheads','acne scars','face wash','skin breakout','teen acne','hormonal acne'],
 ["Wash twice daily with a gentle cleanser, do not pick, and use non-comedogenic moisturiser and sunscreen."],
 ["Products with benzoyl peroxide, salicylic acid or adapalene help mild acne.","See a dermatologist for painful, deep or scarring acne."],['skin']);
E('hairgrowth',"How can I keep my hair healthy?",['hair growth','hair care','hair thinning','grey hair','white hair','hair oil','shampoo','dandruff treatment','hair protein','biotin'],
 ["Healthy hair needs enough protein, iron and vitamins, gentle handling and a clean scalp."],
 ["Dandruff is helped by anti-dandruff shampoo with ketoconazole or zinc.","Sudden or patchy hair loss needs a doctor."],['hair','anemia']);
E('backposture',"How do I stop neck and back pain from sitting?",['neck pain sitting','back pain sitting','desk pain','shoulder tension','text neck','chair posture','sit properly','cervical','spondylosis','sciatica','slip disc','lower back stiffness'],
 ["Pain from sitting comes from long static postures. Change position often."],
 ["Stand and move every 30 to 45 minutes.","Screen at eye level, feet flat, lower back supported.","Strengthen the core and stretch the hips and chest.","Leg numbness or weakness, or loss of bladder control, needs urgent care."],['posture','backpain']);
E('kneecare',"How do I protect my knees?",['knee care','knee pain walking','knee pain stairs','runners knee','knee strengthening','knee exercise','acl','meniscus','knee swelling','knee replacement'],
 ["Strong thigh and hip muscles take load off the knees. Keep a healthy weight and wear good shoes."],
 ["Try straight-leg raises, glute bridges and gentle cycling.","See a doctor for locking, giving way, swelling or pain at night."],['arthritis','strength']);
E('osteoexercise',"What exercise is good for bones?",['bone exercise','weight bearing','bone density exercise','osteoporosis exercise','jumping','stairs bone','prevent fracture'],
 ["Weight-bearing and resistance exercise such as walking, stair climbing and light weights keep bones strong."],
 ["Add calcium and vitamin D and avoid smoking.","Balance work such as tai chi cuts fall risk."],['osteo','strength']);
E('migrainetype',"What triggers migraines?",['migraine trigger','migraine aura','migraine with nausea','light sensitivity','one sided headache','migraine treatment','cluster headache','tension headache','sinus headache'],
 ["Migraine is a throbbing, often one-sided headache with nausea or light sensitivity. Common triggers: poor sleep, skipped meals, stress, dehydration, certain foods and hormones."],
 ["Rest in a dark room, drink water and take pain relief early as the label says.","Keep a diary of triggers.","See a doctor if headaches are frequent, or if a sudden severe one, with fever, stiff neck, weakness or confusion, appears."],['headache','sleep']);
E('vertigo',"Why do I feel the room spinning?",['room spinning','vertigo causes','spinning dizziness','bppv','balance problem','ear dizziness','dizzy when turning','dizzy lying down','motion dizziness'],
 ["True spinning often comes from the inner ear (BPPV), triggered by turning your head or rolling in bed."],
 ["Sit down until it stops and avoid sudden head movements.","See a doctor if it is new, frequent, or comes with hearing loss, double vision, weakness or severe headache."],['dizzy','ear']);
E('fainting',"What should I do if someone faints?",['faint','fainting','fainted','passed out','black out','blackout','syncope','collapse','unconscious person','not responding'],
 ["Lay the person flat and raise their legs about 30 cm. Loosen tight clothes and make sure they can breathe."],
 ["They should recover within a minute. If not, or if they are not breathing normally, call emergency services and start CPR.","Do not give food or drink until fully awake.","Fainting with chest pain, palpitations or during exercise needs urgent medical review."],['cpr','dizzy']);
E('seizure',"What should I do if someone has a seizure?",['seizure','epilepsy','convulsion','convulsions','shaking fit','epileptic'],
 ["Stay calm and time it. Move hard objects away, cushion the head and turn the person on their side once the shaking stops."],
 ["Do not put anything in the mouth or hold them down.","Call emergency services if it lasts more than 5 minutes, repeats, or it is their first seizure."],['cpr','firstaid']);
E('chokingkid',"What do I do if a child is choking?",['child choking','baby choking','infant choking','choking baby','something stuck throat','swallowed object','swallowed coin'],
 ["If a child cannot cough, cry or breathe, call emergency services. For a baby under one: 5 back blows then 5 chest thrusts with two fingers. For a child over one: 5 back blows then 5 abdominal thrusts."],
 ["Never poke blindly in the mouth.","If the child becomes unresponsive, begin CPR.","Take a first-aid course."],['cpr','firstaid']);
E('poison',"What should I do after poisoning or overdose?",['poison','poisoning','overdose','swallowed medicine','swallowed cleaner','ingested','too many tablets','pesticide','kerosene','drug overdose'],
 ["Call emergency services or a poison helpline immediately. Have the container or tablet strip ready."],
 ["Do not make the person vomit unless told to.","Keep them awake and on their side if drowsy.","Store medicines and chemicals out of reach of children."],['firstaid','cpr']);
E('drowning',"What should I do for a drowning or electric shock?",['drowning','drowned','electric shock','electrocution','lightning','shock first aid','water rescue'],
 ["Call emergency services first. Do not touch a person in contact with live current. Switch off the power or use a dry non-metal object to separate them."],
 ["If not breathing, start CPR. For drowning give 5 rescue breaths first if trained.","Anyone shocked, even if they feel fine, should see a doctor because the heart can be affected."],['cpr','firstaid']);
E('burnsevere',"When is a burn serious?",['serious burn','severe burn','burn blisters','chemical burn','hot oil burn','fire burn','burn on face','burn treatment'],
 ["Cool any burn under cool running water for 20 minutes. Remove rings and loose clothing nearby unless stuck."],
 ["Go to hospital for burns bigger than your palm, on the face, hands, feet, genitals or joints, deep or white or charred burns, and any chemical or electrical burn.","Do not use ice, butter, toothpaste or burst blisters."],['firstaid']);
E('bleeding',"How do I stop heavy bleeding?",['heavy bleeding','bleeding wound','stop bleeding','deep cut','blood loss','wound bleeding','bleeding will not stop','tourniquet'],
 ["Press firmly on the wound with a clean cloth and keep pressing. Raise the injured limb if you can."],
 ["Do not remove soaked cloth. Add more on top.","Call emergency services for spurting blood, a deep wound or bleeding that does not slow after 10 minutes.","Seek care for animal bites and dirty wounds."],['firstaid','bites']);
E('headinjury',"When is a head injury serious?",['head injury','hit my head','concussion','head trauma','bump on head','fell on head','knocked out'],
 ["Rest and watch for the next 24 hours. A cold pack helps a bump."],
 ["Go to the emergency department for loss of consciousness, repeated vomiting, worsening headache, confusion, drowsiness, fits, weakness, clear fluid from the nose or ears, or a baby that will not feed.","Avoid sport until symptoms have cleared and a doctor agrees."],['firstaid','fracture']);
E('eyeinjury',"What do I do if something gets in my eye?",['something in eye','eye injury','chemical in eye','eye irritation','dust in eye','eye foreign body','rub eye'],
 ["Do not rub. Rinse the eye with clean running water for 15 minutes, especially after a chemical splash."],
 ["Go to a doctor for pain, a scratch, a stuck object, vision change or a chemical exposure.","Never remove an embedded object."],['eyecare','firstaid']);
E('allergyshock',"What is anaphylaxis?",['anaphylaxis','severe allergy','allergic shock','epipen','swollen lips','swollen tongue','throat swelling','hives breathing','nut allergy','bee allergy'],
 ["Anaphylaxis is a severe allergic reaction with swelling of the face or throat, wheeze, dizziness or collapse, often within minutes of a trigger."],
 ["Call emergency services at once. Use an adrenaline auto-injector if prescribed, and lie the person flat.","Never wait to see if it settles."],['allergy','emsigns']);
E('medsafety',"How do I take medicines safely?",['medicine safety','paracetamol dose','ibuprofen','painkillers','antibiotics','antibiotic course','expired medicine','missed dose','pain killer','aspirin','self medication','paracetamol'],
 ["Read the label, take the stated dose and tell your doctor about all medicines and supplements."],
 ["Do not exceed the paracetamol limit on the label. Too much damages the liver.","Complete an antibiotic course only when a doctor prescribes it. They do not work on viruses.","Avoid ibuprofen and aspirin if you have stomach ulcers, kidney disease or are on blood thinners, unless advised.","Ask a pharmacist about interactions."],['meds','herbs']);
E('travelhealth',"How do I stay healthy while travelling?",['travel health','jet lag','flying heart rate','long flight','dvt','travel sickness','altitude sickness','road trip','travel tips'],
 ["Drink water, move often and sleep on local time to ease jet lag."],
 ["On long flights walk every hour and flex your ankles to lower clot risk.","Carry your medicines and a copy of prescriptions.","Ascend gradually at altitude and learn the signs of altitude sickness."],['altitude','water']);
E('pollutionmask',"How do I protect myself from smoke and dust?",['haze','wildfire','diwali smoke','crop burning','n95','air filter','indoor air','cooking smoke','incense'],
 ["Fine particles raise heart rate and irritate the lungs. Stay indoors on poor air days and use a well-fitting N95 mask outside."],
 ["Ventilate when cooking and use an exhaust fan.","People with asthma, heart disease, children and pregnant women should take extra care."],['pollution','asthma']);
E('workdesk',"How can I stay healthy at a desk job?",['desk job health','office health','sitting job','work from home health','office exercise','desk exercise','stay active at work','long sitting','sedentary lifestyle'],
 ["Break up sitting. Even 2 minutes of movement every half hour helps blood sugar and mood."],
 ["Walk during calls, use stairs and stretch your hips and chest.","Eat lunch away from the screen and drink water.","Take a short PulseSpace reading at midday to check your stress."],['posture','steps']);
E('meditationstart',"How do I start meditation?",['start meditation','how to meditate','meditation for beginners','mindfulness exercise','body scan','guided meditation','mantra','om chanting','meditation benefits','dhyana'],
 ["Sit comfortably, close your eyes and follow your breath. When your mind wanders, gently return."],
 ["Start with 5 minutes a day and build up.","A body scan from head to toe is easy for beginners.","Try the Calm session in PulseSpace and watch your heart rate settle."],['mindful','breathtech']);
E('gratitude',"How can I feel happier day to day?",['feel happier','happiness','be happy','improve mood','boost mood','positive thinking','mood swings fix','cheer up','motivation low','lonely what to do'],
 ["Mood improves with sleep, movement, sunlight, social contact and purpose."],
 ["Walk outside for 20 minutes, call a friend, write three good things at the end of the day.","Limit news and doomscrolling.","If low mood lasts more than two weeks, talk to a doctor."],['lowmood','journaling']);
E('procrastinate',"How do I build a good habit?",['build habit','habit formation','stick to routine','new habit','break bad habit','bad habit','stay consistent','discipline','self control','habit tracker'],
 ["Start tiny, attach the habit to something you already do and track it."],
 ["Make it easy: lay out workout clothes or keep water at hand.","Do not miss twice in a row.","Use the PulseSpace weekly streak to see your consistency."],['motivation','routine']);
E('workshift',"How do I handle night shifts?",['night shift','shift work','rotating shifts','night duty','working nights','sleep after night shift','circadian','body clock'],
 ["Shift work disturbs your body clock. Protect your sleep and light exposure."],
 ["Sleep in a dark, cool room and wear sunglasses on the way home.","Keep meals light at night and caffeine to the first half of the shift.","Expect higher resting heart rate and lower HRV after night shifts."],['sleep','insomnia']);
E('hrvapps',"How does PulseSpace compare with a chest strap?",['chest strap','polar','ecg accuracy','finger vs chest','ppg vs ecg','optical heart rate','ppg','photoplethysmography','how does optical work'],
 ["PulseSpace uses light (PPG) at the fingertip. A chest strap measures the heart's electrical signal and is more precise for beat timing."],
 ["For resting heart rate and trends, finger PPG is good.","HRV from PPG is close but not identical to ECG-based HRV.","Neither diagnoses heart conditions."],['hrvmath','spoacc']);
E('sensorlife',"How long can I leave the sensor on?",['sensor safe','sensor heat','sensor burn','sensor led safe','led eye','sensor radiation','is sensor safe','is it safe','sensor harm'],
 ["The sensor uses low-power red and infrared LEDs, the same as medical pulse oximeters. It is safe for normal spot checks."],
 ["Do not shine it into the eyes.","Remove it if the sensor feels hot or the skin looks irritated.","Use clean, dry fingers."],['ledtune','fingerpos']);
E('sensorclean',"How do I clean the sensor?",['clean sensor','sanitise sensor','sanitize','disinfect','wipe sensor','dirty sensor','sensor hygiene','sharing sensor'],
 ["Wipe the sensor window gently with a soft cloth lightly dampened with 70% isopropyl alcohol, then let it dry."],
 ["Do not submerge the board or use harsh solvents.","Clean it between users."],['sensorlife']);
E('usewebsite',"How do I use PulseSpace?",['how to use','how do i use this','use this website','how does this website work','get started','tutorial','instructions','help me start','first time','what is pulsespace','what does this do'],
 ["PulseSpace has four tabs: Check-in (a few quick questions), Measure (connect the sensor and hold still for 30 seconds), Results (your vitals, readiness and rhythm map) and Journal (saved readings and trends)."],
 ["Plug in the Arduino, open this page in Chrome or Edge, press Connect sensor and choose the port.","After a reading, save it to your journal and ask the coach anything.","You can look at every page before connecting."],['connecthelp','upload']);
E('whatsmetrics',"What does each reading mean?",['all readings','all metrics','what do the numbers mean','explain readings','what are the readings','metrics explained','list of metrics','vitals explained','glossary'],
 ["PulseSpace shows heart rate, SpO₂, perfusion index, signal quality, pulse amplitude, sensor temperature, HRV (RMSSD), stress score and readiness."],
 ["Tap any small circle around the big dial to see its details.","Ask me about any one, for example \"what is perfusion index\".","Type \"explain my readings\" for a summary of your latest."],['rhr','lowspo2','hrvgood']);
E('connecthelp',"Why can't I connect the sensor?",['cannot connect','connect failed','connect problem','not connecting','connect button not working','serial not supported','web serial','no devices found','port busy','access denied','failed to open'],
 ["USB connection needs Chrome or Edge on a computer. The preview inside Claude and phone browsers cannot open USB."],
 ["Download the PulseSpace file and open it in Chrome or Edge.","Close the Arduino Serial Monitor first because only one program can use the port.","Use a data USB cable and check the baud rate is 115200."],['trouble','browser']);
E('whynosignal',"Why does it say no finger or weak signal?",['no finger','finger not detected','weak signal','poor signal','signal lost','signal poor','low signal quality','lost signal','finger lifted','no signal'],
 ["The sensor needs light, steady contact with your fingertip pad."],
 ["Rest the finger lightly on the window. Pressing hard cuts the signal.","Keep still, warm your hands and shade bright light.","If it never detects a finger, lower FINGER_THRESHOLD in the sketch."],['fingerpos','zerobpm']);
E('mistake',"Are my numbers wrong?",['wrong numbers','numbers wrong','strange reading','weird reading','unrealistic','spo2 too low','heart rate too high on sensor','not matching watch','different from watch','different from oximeter','compare with oximeter','false reading'],
 ["A single odd reading is usually a contact or movement problem."],
 ["Measure again at rest with a warm, still hand.","Compare with a manual pulse count.","Different devices can differ by a few beats and one or two SpO₂ points. If you feel unwell, trust symptoms over numbers."],['spoacc','variation']);
E('privacyfree',"Is PulseSpace really free and private?",['is it free','free to use','no cost','cost','price','api key','login','sign up','account','ads','tracking','privacy','data collected','sell my data','is my data safe','offline'],
 ["Yes. It runs entirely in your browser. There is no account, no server and no tracking. Nothing you type or measure is sent anywhere."],
 ["The journal is stored only in your browser if you press Save.","It works offline once the file is open."],['privacy','aboutcoach']);
E('smalltalk1',"Who made you and how do you work?",['who are you','who made you','your name','what is your name','are you human','are you a robot','are you chatgpt','are you gpt','how do you work','how smart are you','are you intelligent'],
 ["I am the PulseSpace Coach. I am a built-in assistant that matches your question to hundreds of written answers about health and your readings. I am not a large AI model and I am not a doctor."],
 ["I work offline and nothing you type leaves this page.","Ask me anything on health, fitness, first aid, food or your sensor."],['aboutcoach']);
E('thanks2',"What else can you do?",['what other things','more topics','list topics','what do you know','topics','categories'],
 ["I cover more than 250 health topics. Use the topic buttons or type your own question."],
 ["Try: \"BMI for 70 kg 170 cm\", \"max heart rate for age 35\", \"BP 130/85\", \"is 55 bpm okay\".","Ask \"what is my average this week\" once you have saved readings."],['usewebsite']);


E('lungs',"How can I improve my lung capacity?",['lung capacity','improve lungs','lung health','lung exercise','breathing capacity','stronger lungs','increase lung','lungs strong','breath holding','spirometer','pursed lip'],
 ["Regular aerobic exercise and slow breathing are the best ways to build lung efficiency."],
 ["Walk briskly, cycle or swim most days, building up slowly.","Practise diaphragmatic breathing and pursed-lip breathing (in through the nose, out slowly through pursed lips).","Do not smoke and avoid polluted air.","Persistent breathlessness or cough needs a doctor."],['breathtech','asthma','pollution']);
E('dinnerideas',"What should I eat for dinner?",['dinner ideas','what to eat at night','night food','light dinner','dinner healthy','late night food','what should i eat at night','healthy dinner','eat before bed','supper'],
 ["Choose a light, early dinner with protein and vegetables, finished two to three hours before bed."],
 ["Ideas: dal with vegetables and one roti, grilled fish or paneer with salad, vegetable soup with curd, khichdi.","Avoid heavy, oily or very spicy food late, which can cause acidity and poor sleep."],['breakfast','acidity','sleep']);
E('dailyexercise',"Can I exercise every day?",['exercise every day','daily exercise','exercise daily','workout every day','gym every day','exercise seven days','train daily','rest day needed'],
 ["Light activity such as walking is fine daily. Hard training needs rest days so muscles and the heart can recover."],
 ["Mix hard and easy days and take at least one full rest day a week.","A high morning pulse and low HRV on PulseSpace can say you need more rest."],['doms','exercise']);
E('nightheart',"Why does my heart race at night?",['heart race at night','heart racing at night','palpitations at night','heart rate at night','night heart rate','heart pounding at night','heartbeat at night','pulse at night','heart beating fast at night','racing heart when lying down','palpitations lying down'],
 ["A pounding heart at night is often noticed more because it is quiet. Common causes are caffeine, alcohol, stress, a heavy late meal, dehydration, reflux, sleep apnea and anxiety."],
 ["Cut caffeine after noon, avoid alcohol and heavy dinners, and try slow breathing.","See a doctor if it is frequent, lasts long, or comes with chest pain, breathlessness or fainting.","Loud snoring with gasping at night may be sleep apnea."],['palp','apnea','caffeine']);
E('acidnight',"How do I stop acidity at night?",['acidity at night','acid at night','heartburn at night','reflux at night','night acidity','acidity lying down','burning chest after dinner','sour burps','acidity remedy'],
 ["Eat dinner at least three hours before lying down, and keep portions small."],
 ["Raise the head of the bed by 10 to 15 cm and sleep on your left side.","Avoid spicy, fried and very sour food, caffeine, alcohol and smoking.","See a doctor for pain that wakes you, difficulty swallowing, vomiting or weight loss."],['acidity','dinnerideas']);
E('exportdata',"How do I export or back up my data?",['export my data','export data','download data','backup journal','back up data','save data','data export','restore journal','import data','transfer data','csv download','move data'],
 ["Open the Journal tab. Download CSV gives a spreadsheet of your readings. Back up saves a file you can restore later with Restore, even on another browser."],
 ["Your journal lives only in this browser, so back it up before clearing browser data.","These downloads work from the downloaded PulseSpace file in Chrome or Edge."],['journalhelp','privacy']);
E('highbpcoffee',"Can I drink coffee with high blood pressure?",['coffee high bp','coffee with high bp','coffee hypertension','tea high bp','caffeine blood pressure','coffee blood pressure'],
 ["Caffeine can raise blood pressure for a few hours, especially if you do not drink it often. If your blood pressure is high or untreated, keep it to one or two cups and do not drink it before measuring."],
 ["Ask your doctor, since advice depends on your readings and medicines.","Decaf or herbal tea are lower-caffeine options."],['bpnormal','coffeecup']);
E('afterfoodtired',"Why do I feel sleepy after eating?",['tired after eating','sleepy after eating','sleepy after lunch','food coma','drowsy after meal','tired after food','sleepy after food','heavy after eating'],
 ["Large or carb-heavy meals can make you sleepy. Blood flow goes to digestion and blood sugar rises and falls."],
 ["Eat smaller meals with protein and vegetables, and take a 10-minute walk afterwards.","Persistent drowsiness after meals, with thirst or frequent urination, is worth a sugar test."],['mealwalk','diabetes','nap']);
E('calorieneeds',"How many calories do I need?",['how many calories should i eat','daily calorie','calorie needs','calories i need','calorie requirement','maintenance calories','calorie deficit','tdee','bmr'],
 ["Most adults need roughly 1,600 to 2,400 calories a day for women and 2,000 to 3,000 for men, depending on size and activity."],
 ["To lose weight slowly, eat about 300 to 500 calories below what keeps your weight steady.","Quality matters as much as quantity: protein, fibre and whole foods keep you full."],['weightlossplan','balanced']);

E('angina',"What is angina?",['angina','chest pain on exertion','chest pain walking','chest pain stairs','heart blockage','blocked artery','coronary artery disease','cad','stent','angioplasty','bypass surgery'],
 ["Angina is chest pressure or pain when the heart muscle does not get enough blood, often on effort and easing with rest. It is a warning of coronary artery disease."],
 ["See a doctor soon for any effort-related chest discomfort.","Pain at rest, lasting over 15 minutes, or with sweating or breathlessness is an emergency.","Treatment includes medicines, lifestyle change, and sometimes a stent or bypass."],['emsigns','chesttight','hearthealth']);
E('heartfailure',"What are the signs of heart failure?",['heart failure','swollen ankles','breathless lying flat','fluid retention','weak heart','cardiomyopathy','ejection fraction','swelling legs','swollen feet','edema'],
 ["Heart failure means the heart pumps less well. Signs are breathlessness, tiredness, swollen ankles or legs, rapid weight gain from fluid and needing extra pillows to sleep."],
 ["See a doctor promptly if you have these. Tests include an echocardiogram.","Treatment includes medicines, less salt and fluid advice, and regular follow-up.","Sudden severe breathlessness needs emergency care."],['bpnormal','salt','emsigns']);
E('murmur',"What is a heart murmur?",['heart murmur','murmur','valve problem','valve disease','mitral','aortic stenosis','hole in heart','congenital heart','rheumatic'],
 ["A murmur is an extra whooshing sound heard with a stethoscope. Many are harmless, especially in children. Some come from valve problems."],
 ["An echocardiogram shows the valves clearly.","See a doctor if you have breathlessness, fainting, chest pain or swelling along with a murmur."],['heartfailure','ecgtest']);
E('ecgtest',"What are ECG, echo and stress tests?",['ecg','ekg','echo','echocardiogram','tmt','treadmill test','stress test','holter','heart test','cardiac test','angiogram','ct angiography','troponin','echo test','what is echo','echo heart'],
 ["ECG records the heart's electrical signal in minutes. Echo is an ultrasound of the heart. A treadmill (stress) test checks the heart during exercise. A Holter is a 24 to 48 hour ECG recorder. Troponin is a blood test for heart muscle injury."],
 ["Your doctor chooses tests from your symptoms and risk.","PulseSpace cannot replace any of these."],['angina','afib']);
E('pacemaker',"What is a pacemaker?",['pacemaker','icd','implanted device','slow heartbeat device','heart block','av block','sick sinus'],
 ["A pacemaker is a small device that keeps the heart from beating too slowly. It is placed under the skin near the collarbone."],
 ["People with pacemakers lead normal lives. Keep strong magnets away from the device and follow check-up schedules.","Dizziness or fainting with a slow pulse should be checked."],['brady','dizzy']);
E('highbpkids',"Can young people have high blood pressure?",['young high bp','bp in 20s','bp at 30','hypertension young','blood pressure in teenagers','family history bp','secondary hypertension'],
 ["Yes. High blood pressure is increasingly seen in people under 40, often linked to weight, salt, stress, alcohol, poor sleep or kidney and hormone problems."],
 ["Check blood pressure at least yearly from your 20s.","Lifestyle changes work well when started early.","A very high reading in a young person deserves a full check-up."],['bpnormal','bplower']);
E('copd',"What is COPD?",['copd','chronic bronchitis','emphysema','smokers cough','lung disease','breathlessness smoker','chronic lung','inhaler for copd'],
 ["COPD is long-term lung damage, mostly from smoking or smoke exposure, causing breathlessness, cough and mucus."],
 ["Stopping smoking is the most important step.","A doctor can confirm it with a breathing test (spirometry) and prescribe inhalers.","Get urgent help for severe breathlessness or blue lips."],['smokingquit','asthma','lowspo2']);
E('pneumonia',"What are signs of pneumonia?",['pneumonia','chest infection','lung infection','cough with fever and breathlessness','green phlegm','rattly chest','sputum','phlegm'],
 ["Pneumonia causes fever, cough with phlegm, chest pain on breathing and breathlessness. It needs a doctor, and sometimes antibiotics."],
 ["Older adults, children and those with other illnesses can get very sick quickly.","Low SpO₂ (below about 94%), fast breathing or confusion means urgent care."],['coldflu','lowspo2','cough']);
E('breathless',"Why am I short of breath?",['short of breath','shortness of breath','breathless','difficulty breathing','out of breath','hard to breathe','cant catch breath','breathing difficulty','breathing problem','breathlessness','gasping'],
 ["Breathlessness can come from fitness, anxiety, asthma, a chest infection, anaemia, heart or lung disease, or being overweight."],
 ["Sudden or severe breathlessness, with chest pain, blue lips or confusion, is an emergency.","Sit upright, loosen clothing and breathe slowly while you get help.","Check your SpO₂ with PulseSpace, but see a doctor even if it looks normal."],['lowspo2','emsigns','asthma']);
E('ibs',"What is irritable bowel syndrome?",['ibs','irritable bowel','stomach cramps and bloating','alternating diarrhea constipation','gas and bloating','spastic colon','bowel problem','stress stomach'],
 ["IBS causes cramps, bloating and changing bowel habits without damage to the gut. Stress and some foods trigger it."],
 ["Keep a food diary, eat regularly, add fibre slowly and manage stress.","See a doctor for blood in stool, weight loss, night symptoms or onset after age 50."],['fibregut','stressmgmt']);
E('appendix',"What are the signs of appendicitis?",['appendicitis','appendix','pain right lower abdomen','right side stomach pain','pain near belly button moving','abdominal pain with fever'],
 ["Appendicitis often starts as pain around the navel that moves to the lower right abdomen, with nausea, loss of appetite and low fever. It gets worse over hours."],
 ["Go to emergency care the same day. Do not take laxatives or heat packs.","Severe, constant or worsening stomach pain always needs a doctor."],['acidity','diarrhea']);
E('gallstones',"What are gallstones?",['gallstone','gallstones','gall bladder','gallbladder','pain after fatty food','upper right abdomen pain','biliary'],
 ["Gallstones can cause pain in the upper right abdomen after fatty meals, with nausea. Often found on ultrasound."],
 ["See a doctor for repeated attacks.","Go to emergency care for severe pain with fever or yellow skin.","Rapid weight loss and very fatty food can trigger attacks."],['jaundice','acidity']);
E('pancreas',"What causes pancreatitis?",['pancreatitis','pancreas','pain after alcohol','pain through to back','amylase','lipase'],
 ["Pancreatitis causes severe upper abdominal pain that may go through to the back, with vomiting. Gallstones and heavy alcohol are common causes."],
 ["It needs urgent hospital care.","Avoid alcohol and very fatty meals."],['gallstones','alcoholcut']);
E('fattyliver',"How do I reverse fatty liver?",['fatty liver','nafld','liver fat','sgot sgpt','liver enzymes','alt ast','liver function test','lft','grade 1 fatty liver'],
 ["Fatty liver is common and often reversible. Losing 7 to 10% of body weight, exercising and cutting sugar and alcohol can clear it."],
 ["Eat more vegetables, whole grains and healthy fats.","Control blood sugar and cholesterol.","Ask your doctor for follow-up liver tests."],['jaundice','weightlossplan','alcoholcut']);
E('hepatitis',"How do I protect myself from hepatitis?",['hepatitis a','hepatitis b','hepatitis c','hep b vaccine','liver infection','hepatitis symptoms','yellow urine'],
 ["Hepatitis A spreads through dirty food and water. Hepatitis B and C spread through blood and body fluids."],
 ["Vaccines protect against A and B.","Do not share needles or razors, and use safe water and food.","Dark urine, yellow eyes and tiredness need a doctor."],['jaundice','vaccines']);
E('stis',"How do I stay safe from sexually transmitted infections?",['std','sti','sexually transmitted','hiv','aids','condom','safe sex','genital','unprotected sex','herpes','syphilis','gonorrhea','chlamydia','hpv'],
 ["Condoms used correctly every time lower the risk of most STIs and HIV. Many infections have no symptoms."],
 ["Get tested regularly if you have new or multiple partners.","HPV vaccine protects against cervical and other cancers.","Treatment for HIV today is very effective. Seek a confidential clinic."],['vaccines']);
E('contraception',"What are the contraception options?",['contraception','birth control','family planning','contraceptive pill','iud','copper t','emergency contraception','morning after pill','condom use','pregnancy prevention','pill side effects'],
 ["Options include condoms, pills, injections, implants, IUDs and sterilisation. Condoms also protect against infections."],
 ["Emergency contraception works best as soon as possible, and up to 3 to 5 days depending on type.","A doctor can help you choose based on your health.","Do not take hormonal pills without advice if you smoke or have clots."],['stis','pregnancycare']);
E('pregnancycare',"How do I have a healthy pregnancy?",['healthy pregnancy','pregnancy care','prenatal','antenatal','folic acid','early pregnancy','pregnancy diet','pregnancy food','what to avoid pregnancy','morning sickness','pregnancy symptoms','first trimester'],
 ["Start folic acid (400 micrograms daily) before conception if possible, eat balanced meals and attend antenatal checks."],
 ["Avoid alcohol, smoking, raw meat and fish, and unpasteurised dairy. Limit caffeine.","Take medicines only on a doctor's advice.","Bleeding, severe pain, reduced baby movement, severe headache or swelling need urgent care.","Morning sickness is common. Small frequent meals and ginger help."],['pregnancyheart','vitamins']);
E('breastfeeding',"Tips for breastfeeding?",['breastfeeding','breast feeding','lactation','milk supply','nursing mother','sore nipples','baby feeding','newborn feeding','how often feed baby','exclusive breastfeeding'],
 ["Breast milk alone is recommended for the first six months. Feed on demand, usually 8 to 12 times a day for newborns."],
 ["A good latch prevents pain. Ask a nurse or lactation consultant for help.","Drink to thirst and eat regularly.","Fever, a hard red breast or poor weight gain in the baby need a doctor."],['kidsfever','vaccinesbaby']);
E('vaccinesbaby',"What vaccines do babies need?",['baby vaccine','childhood vaccines','vaccination schedule','immunization schedule','bcg','polio','mmr','dpt','vaccine chart','missed vaccine','newborn vaccine'],
 ["Children follow a national schedule that begins at birth with BCG, hepatitis B and polio, followed by DPT, rotavirus, pneumococcal, measles and others."],
 ["Keep the vaccination card safe and follow your local schedule.","If a dose is missed, a doctor can catch up without restarting.","Mild fever and soreness after vaccines are common."],['vaccines','kidsfever']);
E('kidsfever',"What should I do for my child's fever?",['child fever','baby fever','kid has fever','toddler fever','fever in infant','child temperature','child cough','child cold','child vomiting','child diarrhea','child not eating'],
 ["Keep the child comfortable, offer fluids and dress lightly. Paracetamol can be given by weight as the label says."],
 ["Take a baby under 3 months with any fever to a doctor immediately.","Seek care for fever over 3 days, a rash, stiff neck, fits, fast breathing, drowsiness or refusing to drink.","Never give aspirin to children."],['fevercare','vaccinesbaby']);
E('colic',"Why does my baby cry so much?",['baby crying','colic','infant crying','baby gas','baby will not sleep','newborn sleep','baby sleep','teething','teething pain','diaper rash','nappy rash','baby rash'],
 ["Crying peaks at 6 to 8 weeks and is usually normal. Check hunger, nappy, temperature and wind, then cuddle and soothe."],
 ["Teething can cause drooling and fussiness. Cold teething rings help.","Nappy rash improves with frequent changes and barrier cream.","See a doctor for fever, vomiting, poor feeding or crying that sounds different."],['breastfeeding','kidsfever']);
E('childgrowth',"Is my child growing normally?",['child growth','child height','child weight','not growing','short height child','underweight child','child development','milestones','late talking','speech delay','autism','adhd','hyperactive'],
 ["Growth and milestones vary. A doctor tracks height, weight and development on charts at check-ups."],
 ["Talk to a paediatrician if your child is not speaking, babbling or making eye contact as expected, or loses skills.","ADHD and autism are assessed by specialists. Early support helps.","Balanced meals and play matter more than supplements."],['kidsfever','vaccinesbaby']);
E('adhd',"What are signs of ADHD?",['adhd in adults','attention deficit','cant focus','distracted easily','impulsive','hyperactivity','restless'],
 ["ADHD causes ongoing inattention, restlessness or impulsiveness that affects daily life, school or work. It also occurs in adults."],
 ["A doctor or psychologist makes the diagnosis. Treatment includes skills coaching and sometimes medicine.","Routines, exercise and sleep help."],['focus','childgrowth']);
E('ocd',"What is OCD?",['ocd','obsessive','compulsive','intrusive thoughts','washing hands too much','checking repeatedly','cleanliness obsession'],
 ["OCD involves unwanted repeating thoughts and rituals that take up time and cause distress. It is common and treatable."],
 ["Therapy (exposure and response prevention) and sometimes medicine work well.","See a doctor or psychologist."],['anxietysym','depression']);
E('bipolar',"What are mood disorders like bipolar?",['bipolar','mania','manic','mood episodes','extreme mood swings','schizophrenia','psychosis','hearing voices','paranoia'],
 ["Bipolar disorder involves swings between low mood and unusually high energy. Psychosis involves losing touch with reality, such as hearing voices."],
 ["These are medical conditions that need a psychiatrist. Treatment works.","If someone is in danger or talks of harming themselves, contact emergency services."],['depression','lowmood']);
E('insomniahelp',"What if I have severe insomnia?",['chronic insomnia','insomnia for months','sleeping pills','sleep medicine','melatonin','cbt for insomnia','cant sleep for days','sleep tablet'],
 ["If poor sleep lasts more than three months, cognitive behavioural therapy for insomnia works better than tablets."],
 ["Sleeping pills are for short-term use only. Ask a doctor.","Melatonin may help jet lag and shift work but is not a cure.","Rule out sleep apnea, thyroid problems, pain and anxiety."],['sleephygiene','apnea']);
E('addiction',"How do I get help for addiction?",['addiction','drug addiction','substance abuse','quit drugs','withdrawal','rehab','gambling addiction','cannabis','weed','marijuana','opioids','heroin','cocaine','pills dependence','tobacco addiction'],
 ["Addiction is a health condition, not a weakness. Help works best with medical and emotional support."],
 ["Do not stop alcohol, sedatives or opioids suddenly without medical advice because withdrawal can be dangerous.","Contact a doctor, a de-addiction centre or a helpline.","Overdose is an emergency: call emergency services."],['alcoholcut','smokingquit','poison']);
E('eczema',"How do I manage eczema or dry itchy skin?",['eczema','atopic','dermatitis','dry itchy skin','itchy skin','skin allergy','contact dermatitis','red itchy patches','moisturiser','scaly skin','hives','urticaria'],
