 ["Do not tilt your head back.","See a doctor if it lasts over 20 minutes, follows a head injury or happens often."],['firstaid','bleeding']);
E('earwax',"Is it safe to clean my ears?",['earwax','ear wax','clean ears','cotton buds','ear cleaning','ear blocked','water in ear','swimmers ear'],
 ["Ears clean themselves. Do not put buds, pins or oil inside."],
 ["Soften wax with a few drops of warm olive oil, or see a doctor to flush it.","Tilt your head to drain water.","Pain, discharge or hearing loss needs a doctor."],['ear','hearing']);
E('vision',"Why is my vision blurry or are floaters normal?",['blurry vision','blurred vision','floaters','double vision','eye floaters','vision problem','night blindness','short sight','myopia','long sight','cataract','glaucoma','squint','eye power'],
 ["Gradual blur is often a need for glasses. Floaters are usually harmless, but a sudden shower of floaters or flashes needs urgent care."],
 ["Sudden vision loss, double vision or eye pain is an emergency.","Cataracts cloud the lens in older age and are treatable. Glaucoma has no early symptoms, so get tested after 40.","Diabetes and high blood pressure can damage the eyes."],['eyes','eyecare']);
E('sinuspain',"Why do I have a facial pain or constant sneezing?",['constant sneezing','runny nose daily','dust allergy','allergic rhinitis','nasal allergy','post nasal drip','throat clearing','facial pressure'],
 ["Allergic rhinitis causes sneezing, itching and a runny nose triggered by dust, pollen or pets."],
 ["Avoid triggers, wash bedding hot, use saline rinses and antihistamines as directed.","See a doctor if it is constant, or with facial pain and fever."],['allergy','sinus']);
E('snoreteeth',"Why do I have bad breath?",['bad breath','halitosis','mouth smell','dry mouth','mouth ulcers','mouth ulcer','canker sore','tongue coating','white tongue','gum bleeding','swollen gums'],
 ["Most bad breath comes from the mouth: plaque, gum disease, a coated tongue or dry mouth."],
 ["Brush the tongue, floss and drink water.","Mouth ulcers heal in 1 to 2 weeks. See a doctor if one lasts over 3 weeks.","Persistent bad breath may be from the throat, nose or stomach."],['oralhealth','dental']);
E('periodontal',"What helps a toothache until I see a dentist?",['toothache relief','tooth pain','tooth abscess','swollen face tooth','wisdom tooth pain','sensitivity','broken tooth','knocked out tooth','root canal'],
