 ["See a doctor if it is new or persistent, or with burning, blood or a weak stream.","Pelvic floor exercises help leakage."],['uti','diabetes']);
E('menshealth',"What health checks do men need?",['mens health','male health','testosterone','low libido','erectile','erectile dysfunction','low sex drive','sperm','infertility male','male fertility','prostate check','psa'],
 ["Men should check blood pressure, blood sugar, cholesterol and weight regularly, and discuss prostate screening from about 50."],
 ["Erectile problems can be an early sign of heart or diabetes issues, so see a doctor.","Fertility depends on both partners. Stop smoking, limit alcohol and keep a healthy weight."],['bp','diabetes','hearthealth']);
E('fertility',"What helps with fertility?",['fertility','trying to conceive','getting pregnant','cant get pregnant','ovulation','conceive','infertility','ivf','irregular cycle pregnancy'],
 ["Most couples conceive within a year. Timing intercourse around ovulation, a healthy weight, no smoking and limited alcohol help."],
 ["See a doctor after 12 months of trying, or 6 months if the woman is over 35.","Folic acid is advised before conception."],['pregnancycare','pcos']);
E('lowlibido',"Why have I lost interest in sex?",['low libido','no interest in sex','sex drive','sexual problems','painful sex','sexual health'],
 ["Stress, tiredness, relationship issues, low mood, some medicines and hormone changes can reduce desire. It is common."],
 ["Talk with your partner and a doctor.","Sleep, exercise and managing stress help.","Pain during sex needs a medical check."],['depression','stressmgmt']);
E('osteoporosis2',"How do I prevent fractures as I age?",['prevent fracture','brittle','fall risk','hip fracture','dexa','bone scan','calcium tablets','osteopenia','spine fracture','stooped back'],
 ["Calcium, vitamin D, weight-bearing exercise, balance work and fall-proofing the home all lower fracture risk."],
 ["A DEXA scan measures bone density.","Remove loose rugs, add grab bars and good lighting."],['osteo','osteoexercise','eldercare']);
E('dementia',"What are early signs of dementia?",['dementia','alzheimers','memory loss','forgetting things','confusion elderly','forgetful old age','mild cognitive','brain health','prevent dementia'],
 ["Dementia involves memory loss and thinking changes that disrupt daily life, beyond normal forgetfulness."],
 ["See a doctor if there is repeated forgetting, getting lost, trouble with familiar tasks or personality change.","Exercise, social activity, blood pressure control, good hearing and sleep protect the brain."],['focus','eldercare']);
E('parkinson',"What are the signs of Parkinson's disease?",['parkinson','tremor','hand tremor','shaking hands','shuffling walk','slow movement','stiffness elderly'],
 ["Early signs include a resting tremor, slowness of movement, stiffness and smaller handwriting."],
 ["See a neurologist. Treatment helps symptoms.","Shaky hands can also come from caffeine, anxiety, thyroid problems or low sugar."],['lowbloodsugar','thyroidsigns']);
E('epilepsyfirst',"Can people with epilepsy live normally?",['epilepsy treatment','epilepsy driving','seizure medicine','seizure triggers','after seizure','febrile seizure','child seizure fever'],
 ["Most people with epilepsy control seizures with regular medicine and lead full lives."],
 ["Do not skip doses. Avoid lack of sleep and alcohol.","A fit with fever in a child (febrile seizure) is usually harmless but needs a doctor."],['seizure']);
E('neckstiff',"When is a headache with neck stiffness an emergency?",['stiff neck fever headache','meningitis','neck stiffness','light hurts eyes fever','rash glass test','worst headache of life','sudden severe headache'],
 ["Fever with severe headache, stiff neck, vomiting or sensitivity to light can be meningitis, and a rash that does not fade under pressure is an emergency."],
 ["Go to a hospital at once.","A sudden worst-ever headache also needs emergency care."],['headache','emsigns']);
E('lowbp',"What if my blood pressure is low?",['low bp symptoms','hypotension','bp low dizzy','bp 90/60','weakness low bp','low blood pressure treatment','salt for low bp'],
 ["Low blood pressure is a problem only if it causes dizziness, fainting or confusion. Dehydration, standing up fast, heat and some medicines are common causes."],
 ["Drink fluids, rise slowly and eat regular meals.","See a doctor for repeated fainting or a sudden drop with illness or bleeding."],['dizzy','pots','hydrationsign']);
E('anemiasym',"What are signs of low iron?",['iron deficiency symptoms','pale','craving ice','hair fall iron','restless legs','cold hands anemia','breathless on stairs','brittle nails','spoon nails'],
 ["Low iron causes tiredness, paleness, breathlessness on effort, hair fall, brittle nails and sometimes restless legs."],
 ["A blood test (haemoglobin, ferritin) confirms it.","Treat the cause, such as heavy periods, and ask about iron tablets."],['anemia','anemiadiet']);
E('bloodtests',"What do common blood test results mean?",['cbc','complete blood count','hemoglobin normal','wbc','platelet normal','esr','crp','tsh normal','creatinine normal','vitamin tests','blood report','lab report','normal range blood','blood test fasting','normal haemoglobin','haemoglobin normal','normal hemoglobin','hemoglobin range','normal platelet count'],
 ["Typical adult ranges (labs differ): haemoglobin 12 to 16 g/dL for women and 13 to 17 for men, white cells 4,000 to 11,000, platelets 150,000 to 450,000, TSH about 0.4 to 4.0 mIU/L, creatinine about 0.6 to 1.2 mg/dL."],
 ["Always use the range printed on your own report.","Fast 8 to 12 hours only for sugar and cholesterol tests unless told otherwise.","A doctor interprets results with your symptoms."],['hba1c','cholnumbers','thyroidsigns']);
E('urinereport',"What do urine tests show?",['urine test','urine routine','urine protein','urine sugar','pus cells','urine culture','cloudy urine','dark urine meaning','foamy urine','red urine'],
 ["Urine tests can show infection (pus cells), sugar, protein, blood and dehydration."],
 ["Cloudy or dark urine often means you need more water.","Red or brown urine, or pain with it, needs a doctor.","Protein in urine can point to kidney problems."],['uti','kidneyhealth']);
E('xray',"Are scans like X-ray, CT and MRI safe?",['xray','x ray','ct scan','mri','ultrasound','radiation','scan safe','pet scan','mammogram','pap smear','colonoscopy','endoscopy','biopsy'],
 ["X-rays and CT use small doses of radiation and are used when the benefit outweighs the risk. Ultrasound and MRI do not use radiation."],
 ["Tell the doctor if you might be pregnant.","Screening tests such as mammograms, Pap smears and colonoscopy find problems early."],['hearthealthnum']);
E('cancersigns',"What are warning signs of cancer?",['cancer','cancer symptoms','cancer signs','lump','breast lump','unexplained weight loss','blood in cough','mole change','persistent hoarseness','tumour','tumor','chemotherapy','cancer prevention','cancer screening'],
 ["Warning signs include a new lump, unexplained weight loss, long-lasting cough or hoarseness, blood in stool, urine or cough, a changing mole and a sore that does not heal."],
 ["Most of these have other causes, but see a doctor if they last more than 2 to 3 weeks.","No tobacco, less alcohol, activity, healthy weight, vaccines and screening lower risk."],['stis','skinsun','hearthealthnum']);
E('breastcheck',"How do I check my breasts?",['breast self exam','breast pain','breast lump check','nipple discharge','breast cancer','mammogram age','breast changes'],
 ["Know how your breasts normally look and feel and report new lumps, skin dimpling, nipple changes or discharge."],
 ["Breast pain alone is usually hormonal.","Ask about mammograms from about 40 to 50, earlier with family history."],['cancersigns','menstrual']);
E('cervical',"What is a Pap smear and HPV vaccine?",['pap smear','cervical cancer','hpv vaccine','cervix','abnormal bleeding','bleeding after sex','white discharge','vaginal discharge','itching vagina','yeast infection','bacterial vaginosis'],
 ["A Pap or HPV test screens for cervical cancer, usually every 3 to 5 years from age 25 to 30. The HPV vaccine prevents most cervical cancers."],
 ["White, odourless discharge is usually normal.","Itching, a strong smell or colour change needs a check.","Bleeding after sex or between periods needs a doctor."],['stis','menstrual']);
E('thyroidpreg',"Why am I gaining or losing weight suddenly?",['sudden weight loss','sudden weight gain','unexplained weight','losing weight without trying','weight gain with tiredness','appetite loss','increased appetite'],
 ["Sudden weight changes can come from thyroid problems, diabetes, stress, depression, medicines or other illnesses."],
 ["See a doctor if you lose more than 5% of your weight in 6 months without trying.","Note appetite, energy and bowel changes."],['thyroidsigns','diabetes']);
E('hotflash',"Why do I feel hot or cold all the time?",['always cold','always hot','feeling cold','feeling hot','cold intolerance','heat intolerance','chills','shivering'],
 ["Feeling unusually cold can point to anaemia, low thyroid, low weight or poor circulation. Feeling hot can point to an overactive thyroid, menopause, infection or anxiety."],
 ["Chills with fever suggest infection.","A blood test for haemoglobin and thyroid is a simple start."],['thyroidsigns','anemiasym']);
E('legs',"Why do my legs swell or ache?",['leg swelling','swollen legs','leg pain walking','varicose veins','calf pain','leg heaviness','blood clot','dvt','restless legs','cramps at night legs','spider veins'],
 ["Leg swelling can come from standing long, heat, pregnancy, heart, kidney or liver problems, or a clot."],
 ["One swollen, red, painful calf may be a clot (DVT) and needs urgent care.","Raise your legs, walk often and avoid long sitting.","Varicose veins are common and treatable."],['heartfailure','travelhealth']);
E('hands',"Why do my hands or wrists hurt?",['hand pain','wrist pain typing','tennis elbow','trigger finger','thumb pain','finger joint pain','mouse pain','repetitive strain','frozen shoulder','shoulder impingement','elbow pain'],
